"""Manually reviewed Mandarin narration; exact numeric fields and bookmarks retain source-context provenance."""

TITLE = '量化金融，从零搭建 · 第39部分：加密货币与去中心化金融'

CHAPTERS = {'Hook': '价格翻倍时，流动性提供者亏多少', 'Chains': '1. 区块链与交易所', 'AMM': '2. 自动做市商', 'LVR': '3. 流动性提供者亏掉了什么', 'Concentrated': '4. 集中流动性', 'MEV': '5. 顺序就是钱', 'Perps': '6. 永续合约', 'Carry': '7. 套利记账与抵押品风险', 'Stable': '8. 稳定币与挤兑', 'Market': '9. 交易场所、基金与横截面', 'House': '10. 第39条规则：清点收益里看不到的风险', 'Research': '写给研究者：相对再平衡损失', 'Outro': '回顾、交易台问题与习题'}

ZH = {
    'Part thirty-nine. Crypto and decentralised finance: markets that never close, exchanges that are programs, futures that never expire, and dollars that are tokens. The closing part of Act six.': '第39部分。加密货币与去中心化金融：永不收盘的市场、本身就是程序的交易所、永不到期的期货，以及以代币形式存在的美元。这是第六幕的最后一部分。',
    "A desk question. <bookmark mark='a'/> Supply equal initial values of ether and dollars to a fee-free constant-product pool, continuously arbitraged to an external price. <bookmark mark='b'/> The ether price doubles. <bookmark mark='c'/> Relative to holding the initial assets, the pool is about five point seven percent behind. That is a valid endpoint comparison. Loss-versus-rebalancing answers a different question: how much value the pool loses against a self-financing portfolio that follows its token holdings at external market prices.": "交易台问题。<bookmark mark='a'/> 向无费常数乘积池存入初始等价值的以太币和美元，并让外部价格持续驱动套利。<bookmark mark='b'/> 以太币价格翻倍。<bookmark mark='c'/> 相对持有原始资产，池仓位落后约5.7%。这是有效的终点比较。再平衡损失回答另一个问题：如果自融资组合跟随池子的代币持仓，却按外部市场价交易，池子相对它损失多少价值？",
    'f"Three questions organize the part. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> On ether\'s twenty twenty-three minute grid, the sum of exact losses divided by each step\'s starting pool value is {lv[\'lvr_pct\']:.2f} percent; squared log increments over eight give {lv[\'rv8_pct\']:.2f}. These are local normalized sums, not a return on fixed initial capital. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> With a fee, the simulator reports arbitrage profit relative to fee-free discrete LVR. Its real-price comparison is descriptive, without proving that fat tails caused a discrepancy from a Brownian approximation. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Finally, carry has a funding and basis ledger, but margin, custody and venue stresses survive a price hedge. We use chosen accounting examples, without historical carry strategy results."': "本部分围绕三个问题。<bookmark mark='a'/> 在以太币2023年的分钟网格上，将精确单步损失除以当步初始池价值再相加，得到 {lv['lvr_pct']:.2f}%；平方对数增量之和除以八为 {lv['rv8_pct']:.2f}%。这是局部归一化之和，不是固定初始资本收益。<bookmark mark='b'/> 有费用时，模拟报告套利利润与无费离散再平衡损失的比。真实价格比较只是描述，并不能证明偏离布朗近似的原因就是厚尾。<bookmark mark='c'/> 最后，套利持仓有资金费与基差记账，但价格对冲不能消除保证金、托管和场所压力。我们使用指定算术例子，不报告历史套利策略业绩。",
    "Why it matters. <bookmark mark='a'/> Crypto links spot tokens, leveraged contracts, stablecoins and investment funds, so failures can cross instruments and venues. <bookmark mark='b'/> Public blockchains expose transactions and contract state, but private order flow, off-chain exchange quotes and economic identities can remain hidden. This is a useful laboratory with incomplete observations. <bookmark mark='c'/> The House's proposed desk needs to connect market risk with custody, smart contracts, collateral and redemption access. A public ledger does not make all of those risks observable or remove intermediaries.": "为何重要？<bookmark mark='a'/> 加密市场连接现货代币、杠杆合约、稳定币和投资基金，失败可以跨工具与场所传播。<bookmark mark='b'/> 公链公开交易与合约状态，但私有订单流、链下交易所报价及经济身份仍可能隐藏。这是观测不完整的实验室。<bookmark mark='c'/> 拟议交易台必须把市场风险与托管、智能合约、抵押品和赎回通道联系起来。公开账本并不让所有风险可见，也不消除中介。",
    'Where this sits. Parts thirty-five to thirty-eight built the dealer, the book, the executor and the market maker. This part finds each of them again in crypto, and closes Act six before Act seven turns to the system as a whole: risk, leverage and crises.': '这一部分的位置。第35到38部分搭建了交易商、订单簿、执行者和做市商。这一部分在加密市场里把它们一一重新找出来，并为第六幕收尾，随后第七幕转向整个体系：风险、杠杆与危机。',
    "A selected timeline through twenty twenty-five. Nakamoto's Bitcoin paper appeared in twenty oh eight; Mt. Gox failed in twenty fourteen; Ethereum launched in twenty fifteen; BitMEX introduced its perpetual in twenty sixteen. <bookmark mark='a'/> Uniswap launched in twenty eighteen. Flash Boys two point oh appeared as a preprint in twenty nineteen and at the security conference in twenty twenty, when decentralized finance expanded. Concentrated liquidity arrived in twenty twenty-one. <bookmark mark='b'/> Terra and FTX failed in twenty twenty-two, when Ethereum also moved to proof of stake. USD coin lost its peg during the Silicon Valley Bank failure in twenty twenty-three. American spot Bitcoin exchange-traded products were approved in January twenty twenty-four; the GENIUS Act became law in July twenty twenty-five. Dates describe selected historical events, not a current regulatory certification.": "选取截至2025年的历史。中本聪2008年发表比特币论文；Mt. Gox于2014年失败；以太坊2015年上线；BitMEX于2016年推出永续合约。<bookmark mark='a'/> Uniswap于2018年上线。Flash Boys 2.0在2019年成为预印本，2020年发表于安全会议，同年去中心化金融扩张；集中流动性于2021年出现。<bookmark mark='b'/> Terra和FTX于2022年失败，以太坊同年转向权益证明。2023年硅谷银行失败期间，USDC脱锚。美国现货比特币交易所交易产品于2024年1月获批；GENIUS法案于2025年7月成法。这些是选定历史事件，不是当前监管认证。",
    'The plan: blockchains, venues and custody; pools and two loss benchmarks; concentrated liquidity and a contextual-bandit simulation; ordering and transaction attacks; perpetual funding and carry accounting; stablecoin redemption and run mechanisms; then the assumptions and proof of loss-versus-rebalancing. We will distinguish exact accounting identities, continuous-price limits, simulated policies and descriptive market observations, because their evidence supports different conclusions.': '安排如下：链、场所与托管；流动性池与两个损失基准；集中流动性及上下文赌博机模拟；排序与交易攻击；永续资金费及套利记账；稳定币赎回与挤兑机制；最后是再平衡损失的假设与证明。我们区分精确恒等式、连续价格极限、模拟策略和市场描述，因为它们支持的结论不同。',
    'In the House, a digital-assets desk opens, the last of the trading desks. Its first task is to learn which of its risks its returns will never show.': '在本系列公司里，数字资产交易台开张了，这是最后一个交易台。它的第一项任务是弄清楚，它的哪些风险永远不会出现在它的收益里。',
    'Chapter one. Crypto markets trade on two kinds of venue at once: exchanges that look like the ones of Parts thirty-five to thirty-eight, and programs on a public ledger that need no exchange at all. Both run every hour of every day.': '第1章。加密市场同时在两类场所交易：一类交易所看起来和第35到38部分的一样，另一类是公共账本上的程序，根本不需要交易所。两者都全天候运行。',
    "A blockchain is a public ledger. <bookmark mark='a'/> Anyone can read it and anyone can propose transactions, which are gathered into blocks. <bookmark mark='b'/> Each block commits to the one before it, so changing the past means redoing everything since. <bookmark mark='c'/> And programs live on it too. A trading pool is a contract that holds tokens and follows its formula, with no one in between.": "区块链是一个公共账本。<bookmark mark='a'/>任何人都可以读取它，任何人都可以提交交易，交易被打包成区块。<bookmark mark='b'/>每个区块都承诺了它之前的那个区块，所以改写过去意味着重做此后的一切。<bookmark mark='c'/>程序也存在于它之上。一个交易池就是一份智能合约，持有代币、按它的公式运行，中间没有任何人。",
    "Who writes the ledger. <bookmark mark='a'/> Bitcoin targets a block about every ten minutes; proof-of-work chain selection follows cumulative work among valid chains. <bookmark mark='b'/> Since the September twenty twenty-two Merge, Ethereum uses proof of stake and twelve-second slots, some of which can be missed. Finality requires validator votes and can be delayed. <bookmark mark='c'/> Gas measures computation. Inclusion pays a protocol base fee and priority fees under the applicable rules, rather than one undifferentiated auction. <bookmark mark='d'/> Builders and proposers influence inclusion and order, subject to transaction validity and their arrangements.": "谁写账本？<bookmark mark='a'/> 比特币目标是约每十分钟一块；在有效链中，工作量证明按累计工作量选择链。<bookmark mark='b'/> 2022年9月合并后，以太坊采用权益证明和12秒时隙，部分时隙会错过。最终性需要验证者投票，也可能延迟。<bookmark mark='c'/> Gas衡量计算，纳入区块的费用包含适用规则下的协议基础费与优先费，并非一个不加区分的拍卖。<bookmark mark='d'/> 构建者与提议者影响纳入和排序，但受到交易有效性及其安排约束。",
    "Two venue families. <bookmark mark='a'/> Centralized venues generally hold customer assets and match orders in off-chain books; products and custody arrangements vary. <bookmark mark='b'/> Decentralized venues execute through contracts. Automated market makers are one design, but on-chain order books and hybrid designs also exist. Users retain keys until execution while pooled assets remain exposed to contracts and any administrative controls. <bookmark mark='c'/> Stablecoins, bridges and arbitrageurs connect venues. Public settlement does not eliminate custody, oracle, contract or execution risk.": "两类场所。<bookmark mark='a'/> 中心化场所通常持有客户资产，在链下订单簿撮合；产品与托管安排各异。<bookmark mark='b'/> 去中心化场所通过合约执行。自动做市是一种设计，链上订单簿和混合设计也存在。用户在执行前保留密钥，但池中资产仍暴露于合约及任何管理控制。<bookmark mark='c'/> 稳定币、桥和套利者连接这些场所。公开结算并不消除托管、预言机、合约或执行风险。",
    "A market with continuous calendar time. <bookmark mark='a'/> A non-leap year has eight thousand seven hundred sixty hours; a six-and-a-half-hour stock session over two hundred fifty-two days gives about sixteen hundred thirty-eight. Actual venues can halt or become inaccessible. <bookmark mark='b'/> Weekend liquidity varies by venue, period and product; a historical comparison does not establish a constant half-volume rule. <bookmark mark='c'/> For comparable independent daily increments, volatility scales with the square root of three hundred sixty-five calendar days. Serial dependence, jumps and changing liquidity require a richer model. A calendar convention alone does not predict when the largest move will occur.": "连续日历时间的市场。<bookmark mark='a'/> 平年有8760小时；每天6.5小时、每年252天的股票交易时段约1638小时。实际场所仍可能暂停或无法访问。<bookmark mark='b'/> 周末流动性随场所、时期和产品而变；历史比较不能建立固定减半规律。<bookmark mark='c'/> 对可比、独立的日增量，波动率按365个日历日的平方根缩放。有序列依赖、跳跃和变化的流动性时需要更丰富模型。日历约定本身不能预测最大波动何时出现。",
    "And the plumbing. <bookmark mark='a'/> A centralised crypto exchange is broker, venue and clearing house at once, roles that Parts twenty-one and thirty-five kept apart. <bookmark mark='b'/> Margin is marked continuously and positions are liquidated by machine, Part two's margin account. <bookmark mark='c'/> If a liquidation cannot be filled, the exchange's insurance fund pays; when it runs out, profitable positions on the other side are cut, which is called auto-deleveraging.": "还有底层管道。<bookmark mark='a'/>中心化加密交易所同时是经纪商、交易场所和清算所，这些角色在第21和35部分是分开的。<bookmark mark='b'/>保证金被持续盯市，仓位由机器强制平仓，也就是第2部分的保证金账户。<bookmark mark='c'/>如果一笔强平无法成交，由交易所的保险基金赔付；保险基金用完后，另一边盈利的仓位会被削减，这叫自动减仓。",
    'f"The failure that defined the risk: FTX, in November twenty twenty-two, as reported and as later established at trial. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> FTX\'s own token, FTT, opened the month at about {f[\'first\']:.0f} dollars on Binance. A news report questioned the balance sheet of its affiliated trading firm, Alameda, much of it held in FTT; Binance said it would sell its own FTT. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Withdrawals stopped on the eighth, and the token fell to about {f[\'low\']:.2f} dollars. Customer assets had been used by the affiliate; its founder was convicted of fraud in November twenty twenty-three."': "定义了这种风险的那次倒闭：2022年11月的FTX，据报道，并经后来的庭审确认。<bookmark mark='a'/>FTX自己的代币FTT，月初在币安上约为{f['first']:.0f}美元。一篇新闻报道质疑其关联交易公司Alameda的资产负债表，其中大量资产就是FTT；币安表示将卖出自己持有的FTT。<bookmark mark='b'/>8日提现停止，该代币跌到约{f['low']:.2f}美元。客户资产曾被关联公司动用；其创始人于2023年11月被判欺诈罪成立。",
    "Three lessons. <bookmark mark='a'/> Venue risk is not in the returns: a strategy run on FTX looked normal until the day it was gone, and no backtest contains that day. <bookmark mark='b'/> Collateral is the exposure: margin and spot held at a venue are lost with it, so the House caps them by venue, the way Part twenty-one priced counterparty exposure. <bookmark mark='c'/> And a balance sheet built on the issuer's own token is worth what that token fetches in a fire sale.": "三条教训。<bookmark mark='a'/>交易场所风险不在收益里：一个在FTX上运行的策略，直到资产消失的那一天之前看起来都很正常，而没有任何回测包含那一天。<bookmark mark='b'/>抵押品就是敞口：存放在交易场所的保证金和现货会随它一起损失，所以本系列公司按场所设定上限，就像第21部分为交易对手敞口定价那样。<bookmark mark='c'/>而建立在发行方自家代币上的资产负债表，只值那个代币在甩卖中能卖出的价钱。",
    "The cash leg needs its own exposure map. <bookmark mark='a'/> Reserve-backed tokens such as tether and USD coin offer specified redemption rights, usually subject to customer eligibility and issuer terms. <bookmark mark='b'/> Deposits, bills and repo can support reserves, but legal claims, access timing and other liabilities matter. The token is not automatically an insured bank deposit. <bookmark mark='c'/> BTCUSDT is a bitcoin quote in tether, not directly in dollars. Treat quote-currency exposure separately from the token being traded and verify the actual issuer's terms.": "现金腿也需要暴露地图。<bookmark mark='a'/> USDT和USDC等储备支持代币提供指定赎回权，通常受客户资格与发行人条款限制。<bookmark mark='b'/> 存款、国债和回购可支持储备，但法律请求权、通道时序及其他负债仍重要。代币不自动等于有保险的银行存款。<bookmark mark='c'/> BTCUSDT是以USDT计价的比特币，不是直接美元报价。把计价币风险与所交易代币分开，核查实际发行人条款。",
    'Pause and predict. A pool holds five thousand ether and ten million dollars, so its price is two thousand. A trader buys five hundred ether from it, paying a fee of three tenths of a percent. What is the average price paid?': '暂停并预测。一个池子持有五千个以太币和一千万美元，所以价格是两千美元。一位交易者从中买入五百个以太币，支付千分之三的手续费。平均成交价是多少？',
    'f"Chapter two, and the answer to the pause: about {t[\'avg\']:,.0f} dollars per ether on average, {100 * t[\'slip\']:.0f} percent above the pool\'s starting price. A pool has no order book, only a formula, and the formula charges more for every additional unit. This chapter takes the formula apart."': "第2章，以及暂停问题的答案：平均每个以太币约{t['avg']:,.0f}美元，比池子的起始价格高{100 * t['slip']:.0f}%。池子没有订单簿，只有一个公式，而公式对每多买一单位都要价更高。这一章把这个公式拆开来看。",
    "The fee-adjusted constant-product swap. <bookmark mark='a'/> A pool has token reserve x and numeraire reserve y. Without fees, swaps follow a fixed product. <bookmark mark='b'/> Its infinitesimal pre-fee token price is y over x, the negative slope of the reserve curve. <bookmark mark='c'/> If gross token input is delta x and input fee is f, only one minus f times delta x enters the invariant, giving the displayed output. <bookmark mark='d'/> In a native fee-retaining pool, the actual reserve product grows as fees accumulate. The lecture's arbitrage simulator instead keeps its curve fixed and accounts for fees outside it. Those are distinct conventions, so its results are not a complete replay of native Uniswap fee compounding.": "考虑费用后的常数乘积交换。<bookmark mark='a'/> 池有代币储备x和计价币储备y，无费交换沿固定乘积曲线进行。<bookmark mark='b'/> 无穷小、费前的代币价格是y除以x，即储备曲线斜率的负值。<bookmark mark='c'/> 总代币输入为delta x、费率为f时，只有一减f乘以delta x进入不变量，输出由式子给定。<bookmark mark='d'/> 原生池若保留费用，实际储备乘积随费用积累增长。本讲套利模拟却保持曲线固定，把费用另记在曲线外。两种口径不同，模拟不是原生Uniswap费用复投的完整重放。",
    'f"A pool of {a[\'x\']:,.0f} ether and {y_m:.0f} million dollars of a dollar stablecoin, so a price of two thousand. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> A buyer of ether moves the point up the curve: ether leaves, dollars arrive, and the slope, the price, rises. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> A seller moves it back down. The curve never runs out: it simply asks a higher price for every further unit, without limit."': "一个持有{a['x']:,.0f}个以太币和{y_m:.0f}百万美元稳定币的池子，所以价格是两千。<bookmark mark='a'/>以太币的买家把这个点沿曲线向上推：以太币流出，美元流入，斜率也就是价格随之上升。<bookmark mark='b'/>卖家把它推回去。这条曲线永远不会耗尽：它只是对每多一单位要价更高，没有上限。",
    'f"What the curve charges. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Ten ether cost {100 * t0[\'slip\']:.1f} percent above the starting price: mostly the fee. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> A hundred, {100 * a[\'trades\'][1][\'slip\']:.1f} percent; five hundred, a tenth of the pool, {100 * a[\'trades\'][2][\'slip\']:.0f} percent; <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> and a thousand, a fifth of the pool, {100 * t3[\'slip\']:.0f} percent. Slippage grows faster than size, because the trade walks along a curve that steepens. It is Part thirty-six\'s order book, with the depth set by a formula instead of by makers."': "曲线收多少钱。<bookmark mark='a'/>十个以太币比起始价格贵{100 * t0['slip']:.1f}%，主要是手续费。<bookmark mark='b'/>一百个，{100 * a['trades'][1]['slip']:.1f}%；五百个，即池子的十分之一，{100 * a['trades'][2]['slip']:.0f}%；<bookmark mark='c'/>一千个，即池子的五分之一，{100 * t3['slip']:.0f}%。滑点比规模增长得更快，因为交易沿着一条越来越陡的曲线前进。这就是第36部分的订单簿，只是深度由公式而不是由做市商决定。",
    "The general form. <bookmark mark='a'/> A constant-function market maker accepts any trade that keeps an invariant fixed, with convex level sets. <bookmark mark='b'/> Its price is the slope of the level set. <bookmark mark='c'/> Balancer's weighted pools keep a fixed share of their value in each token. <bookmark mark='d'/> And Curve's stableswap, for assets meant to trade at par, is almost a straight line near the peg, so stablecoin swaps barely move the price, and bends sharply when the peg is lost.": "一般形式。<bookmark mark='a'/>恒定函数做市商接受任何保持某个不变量固定的交易，其等值线是凸的。<bookmark mark='b'/>它的价格是等值线的斜率。<bookmark mark='c'/>Balancer的加权池在每种代币上保持固定的价值份额。<bookmark mark='d'/>Curve的stableswap用于本应平价交易的资产，在锚定点附近几乎是一条直线，所以稳定币兑换几乎不改变价格，而一旦脱锚就急剧弯曲。",
    "How the pool's price stays right. <bookmark mark='a'/> The pool does not know the market price; it only knows its reserves. When ether rises on a centralised exchange, the pool still quotes the old price. <bookmark mark='b'/> Arbitrageurs buy the cheap ether from the pool and sell it elsewhere, until the pool's price, net of its fee, matches the market. <bookmark mark='c'/> Every such trade is made against a stale price, like the sniped quotes of Part thirty-eight: the arbitrageur's profit is the liquidity providers' loss.": "池子的价格如何保持正确。<bookmark mark='a'/>池子不知道市场价格，它只知道自己的储备。当以太币在中心化交易所上涨时，池子仍然报旧价。<bookmark mark='b'/>套利者从池子买入便宜的以太币，再到别处卖出，直到池子扣除手续费后的价格与市场一致。<bookmark mark='c'/>每一笔这样的交易都是对着过时的价格做的，就像第38部分被狙击的报价：套利者的利润就是流动性提供者的损失。",
    "A pool can be used as a price input, but the observation rule matters. <bookmark mark='a'/> For a fee-free fixed-product move that multiplies pool price by r, the token reserve falls by root r and the numeraire reserve rises by root r. Gross input is not the attacker's net loss or profit. <bookmark mark='b'/> Arithmetic TWAP averages prices over time. <bookmark mark='c'/> Averaging log prices and exponentiating gives a geometric time average instead; an integral of log price alone is not either price-level average. <bookmark mark='d'/> Flash loans require atomic repayment. They can relax upfront capital needs, but fees, gas, impact, competing arbitrage and oracle safeguards still matter. An attack's profitability needs a full transaction and valuation model.": "池可作为价格输入，但观察规则重要。<bookmark mark='a'/> 无费固定乘积池价格乘r时，代币储备除以根号r，计价币储备乘根号r。总输入不是攻击者净损失或净利润。<bookmark mark='b'/> 算术时间均价对价格水平作时间平均。<bookmark mark='c'/> 先平均对数价格再取指数，得到几何时间均价；对数积分本身不是这两种价格水平均值。<bookmark mark='d'/> 闪电贷需要原子偿还，可放松预先资本要求，却仍有费用、gas、冲击、套利竞争和预言机保护。攻击盈利需要完整交易及估值模型。",
    'f"What a liquidity provider gives up. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> At price P the constant-product pool holds the square root of k over P of the token, and is worth two root k P. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Simply holding the starting assets would be worth the start times r plus one, where r is the price ratio. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Their ratio, minus one, is the impermanent loss: two root r over one plus r, minus one. <bookmark mark=\'d\'/> If ether doubles, the pool is worth {100 * abs(a[\'il2\']):.1f} percent less than holding: the desk question\'s answer. A halving costs exactly the same."': "流动性提供者放弃了什么。<bookmark mark='a'/>价格为P时，恒定乘积池持有根号k除以P的代币，价值为二倍根号kP。<bookmark mark='b'/>单纯持有起始资产的价值是起点乘以r加一，其中r是价格之比。<bookmark mark='c'/>两者之比减一就是无常损失：二倍根号r除以一加r，再减一。<bookmark mark='d'/>如果以太币翻倍，池子比持有少值{100 * abs(a['il2']):.1f}%：这就是交易台问题的答案。价格减半的代价完全一样。",
    'f"The whole curve. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Small for small moves, symmetric in the logarithm of the price, and {100 * abs(a[\'il4\']):.0f} percent at a fourfold move either way. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> It is called impermanent because it vanishes if the price returns to where it started. That name is the problem: it depends only on where the price ends, not on the path, so it says nothing about how much the pool paid to arbitrageurs along the way, or whether the fees covered it."': "整条曲线。<bookmark mark='a'/>小幅变动时很小，对价格的对数对称，价格四倍变动时为{100 * abs(a['il4']):.0f}%，无论涨跌。<bookmark mark='b'/>它被称为“无常”，是因为价格回到起点时它就消失了。这个名字恰恰是问题所在：它只取决于价格最终停在哪里，而不取决于路径，所以它完全不告诉你池子一路上付给了套利者多少钱，也不告诉你手续费是否弥补了这些。",
    "Pause and predict. In twenty twenty-three ether rose from about twelve hundred dollars to twenty-three hundred. A constant-product pool was arbitraged to Binance's price every minute. What share of its value did it lose to arbitrageurs, against a portfolio that held the same ether but traded at market prices?": '暂停并预测。2023年，以太币从约一千二百美元涨到二千三百美元。一个恒定乘积池每分钟都被套利到币安的价格。和一个持有相同数量以太币、但按市场价格交易的组合相比，它把自身价值的多大比例输给了套利者？',
    'f"Chapter three. On the minute grid, the sum of exact step losses divided by each step\'s starting pool value is {lv[\'lvr_pct\']:.1f} percent. This changing-denominator sum is not a total return on initial capital. Impermanent loss compares the endpoint with holding initial assets; loss-versus-rebalancing uses a different self-financing benchmark. We need both comparisons and their assumptions."': "第三章。在分钟网格上，各步精确损失除以当步初始池价值再求和，得到 {lv['lvr_pct']:.1f}%。这个分母变化的和不是初始资本总收益。无常损失将终点与持有原始资产比较；再平衡损失使用另一个自融资基准。我们需要两种比较及各自假设。",
    "Three portfolios. <bookmark mark='a'/> Hold: the starting assets, kept. <bookmark mark='b'/> The pool, which sells the token as it rises and buys as it falls, at its own stale price. <bookmark mark='c'/> And the rebalancing portfolio of Jason Milionis, Ciamac Moallemi, Tim Roughgarden and Anthony Lee Zhang: the same holdings as the pool at every instant, but every adjustment made at the market price.": "三个组合。<bookmark mark='a'/>持有：保留起始资产。<bookmark mark='b'/>池子：价格上涨时卖出代币、下跌时买入，用的都是它自己过时的价格。<bookmark mark='c'/>以及Jason Milionis、Ciamac Moallemi、Tim Roughgarden和Anthony Lee Zhang的再平衡组合：每一时刻的持仓都与池子相同，但每一次调整都按市场价格进行。",
    'f"Ether in twenty twenty-three, a constant-product pool with no fee, arbitraged to Binance\'s price every ten minutes. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Holding the starting assets ended at {pth[\'hold\'][-1]:.3f} of the start. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> The rebalancing portfolio, at {pth[\'rebal\'][-1]:.3f}. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> The pool, at {pth[\'lp\'][-1]:.3f}: below both, and the gap to the rebalancing portfolio widens steadily, through calm and rally alike."': "2023年的以太币，一个不收手续费的恒定乘积池，每十分钟被套利到币安的价格。<bookmark mark='a'/>持有起始资产最终为起点的{pth['hold'][-1]:.3f}。<bookmark mark='b'/>再平衡组合为{pth['rebal'][-1]:.3f}。<bookmark mark='c'/>池子为{pth['lp'][-1]:.3f}：低于两者，而且与再平衡组合的差距稳步扩大，无论市场平静还是上涨。",
    'f"Take differences in units of initial value. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Pool minus hold is {il:+.3f}; divide this gap by terminal hold value to recover the standard relative impermanent-loss percentage. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Pool minus the common-initial-value rebalancing portfolio is {-lvr:+.3f}. On this grid, the benchmark holds the pool\'s previous-step token amount over each external price move, without fees. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Rebalancing minus hold is {mk:+.3f}, an exposure difference. Hedging it in practice adds funding, execution, collateral and timing costs; the accounting decomposition alone does not make those costs disappear."': "以初始价值为单位作差。<bookmark mark='a'/> 池减持有为 {il:+.3f}；再除以期末持有价值，才得到标准相对无常损失百分比。<bookmark mark='b'/> 池减共同初值的再平衡组合为 {-lvr:+.3f}。在此网格中，基准在每次外部价格变动期间持有池子前一步的代币量，且无费用。<bookmark mark='c'/> 再平衡减持有为 {mk:+.3f}，是暴露差异。现实对冲会加入资金费、执行、抵押品和时序成本；记账分解本身不能让成本消失。",
    "Why use this benchmark? <bookmark mark='a'/> With common initial wealth, the self-financing rebalancing portfolio follows the pool's token holdings while trading at the external price. In an ideal continuous, frictionless model, offsetting that token exposure isolates the loss term. <bookmark mark='b'/> The continuous loss depends on the whole path through volatility and the pool's curvature; an endpoint alone does not determine it. With jumps or discrete trading, finite-step terms matter. <bookmark mark='c'/> Arbitrage profits, fees and ordering payments are related but distinct ledgers. Their equality needs a specified mechanism and common units, rather than a general claim that every measured loss has one recipient.": "为什么用这个基准？<bookmark mark='a'/> 从共同初始财富出发，自融资组合跟随池子的代币量，但按外部价格交易。理想连续无摩擦模型下，抵消代币暴露可隔离损失项。<bookmark mark='b'/> 连续损失通过波动和曲率依赖整条路径；终点不能单独决定它。跳跃和离散交易还涉及有限步长项。<bookmark mark='c'/> 套利利润、费用和排序付款相互关联，却是不同账目。等式需要指定机制与一致单位，不能笼统声称每一单位损失只有一个收款者。",
    'f"For a smooth fee-free constant-product pool arbitraged continuously against a continuous semimartingale price, the local loss rate is variance over eight times current pool value. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Realized squared log increments on ether\'s selected twenty twenty-three grid give a volatility scale of {100 * lv[\'vol\']:.0f} percent. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Their sum divided by eight is {lv[\'rv8_pct\']:.2f} percent. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> The sum of exact discrete losses normalized by each starting pool value is {lv[\'lvr_pct\']:.2f} percent. Close numbers describe a small-increment relation on this sample; they neither establish a continuous price model nor represent a compounded LP return."': "光滑、无费常数乘积池持续对连续半鞅价格套利时，局部损失速率是方差除以八再乘当前池价值。<bookmark mark='a'/> 以太币选定2023年网格的平方对数增量给出约 {100 * lv['vol']:.0f}% 的波动尺度。<bookmark mark='b'/> 平方和除以八为 {lv['rv8_pct']:.2f}%。<bookmark mark='c'/> 各步精确离散损失按当步初始池价值归一化后之和为 {lv['lvr_pct']:.2f}%。相近数字描述该样本的小增量关系，既不确立连续价格模型，也不是复利LP收益。",
    'f"Sampling matters. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> On this one price history, the local normalized loss sums on minute, five-minute, hourly and daily grids range from {lo:.2f} to {hi:.2f} percent. Each grid uses different endpoints and misses its within-step price path. These similar totals are a sample finding, not a theorem that arbitrage frequency is irrelevant. Microstructure noise, jumps, omitted intraperiod variation and fee bands can change the comparison. The continuous variance formula is a limit under specified assumptions."': "采样频率重要。<bookmark mark='a'/> 同一价格历史中，分钟、五分钟、小时和日网格的局部归一化损失和介于 {lo:.2f}% 与 {hi:.2f}% 之间。各网格使用不同端点并漏掉步内路径。总量相近是样本发现，不是套利频率无关的定理。微观结构噪声、跳跃、漏掉的期内变化与费用带均会改变比较。连续方差公式是特定假设下的极限。",
    'f"A useful first hurdle matches units. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> In an ideal token-hedged, fee-free reference calculation, fees must offset loss-versus-rebalancing plus all hedge and operating costs. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> A constant fee times turnover measured against the same contemporaneous capital gives fee yield. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Dividing the sample\'s normalized loss sum by a three-tenths-percent fee gives about {need:.0f} capital turns for the year, <bookmark mark=\'d\'/> or {per_day:.1f} percent per calendar day if spread evenly. This is a rough changing-capital turnover hurdle, not a validated fixed-initial-capital break-even strategy. Fee bands change trades and holdings; arbitrage fees must be reconciled with their own loss ledger."': "先匹配单位。<bookmark mark='a'/> 理想代币对冲、无费参考计算中，费用应抵消再平衡损失及所有对冲、运营成本。<bookmark mark='b'/> 固定费率乘以按同期资本计量的周转，给出费用收益率。<bookmark mark='c'/> 将样本归一化损失和除以0.3%费率，全年约需 {need:.0f} 次资本周转，<bookmark mark='d'/> 若平均摊开，每日约为池价值的 {per_day:.1f}%。这是分母变化的粗略周转门槛，不是经验证的初始资本盈亏平衡策略。费用带改变交易及持仓，套利费还须与自己的损失账目核对。",
    "The same thing in Part eleven's language. <bookmark mark='a'/> A pool's value is concave in the price: it is short gamma, like a written straddle. <bookmark mark='b'/> A hedged option seller pays half gamma times variance, and a hedged liquidity provider pays exactly that. <bookmark mark='c'/> Its fees play the role of the option's time decay. Providing liquidity to a pool is selling volatility.": "用第11部分的语言再说一遍。<bookmark mark='a'/>池子的价值是价格的凹函数：它是负伽马，就像卖出的跨式期权。<bookmark mark='b'/>做了对冲的期权卖方支付伽马的一半乘以方差，而做了对冲的流动性提供者支付的正是这个。<bookmark mark='c'/>它的手续费扮演期权时间衰减的角色。为池子提供流动性就是在卖波动率。",
    'Pause and predict. Choose a multiplicative range from P divided by one point zero five to one point zero five times P. At its geometric centre, how many times as much liquidity per dollar does it provide as a full-range constant-product position? What happens to local loss per dollar while the position is in range? Distinguish this centre comparison from its realized fee income over a whole path.': '暂停预测。选择从P除以1.05到1.05乘P的乘法区间。在几何中心，它每美元提供的流动性是全区间常数乘积仓位的多少倍？仓位处于区间内时，每美元局部损失如何变化？把中心比较与整条路径的实际费用收入区分开。',
    "f'Chapter four, and the answer to the pause: about {e5:.0f} times as much liquidity per dollar, and so about {e5:.0f} times the loss to arbitrage per dollar, as long as the price stays inside the range. Concentration is leverage on the same short-volatility position.'": '第4章，以及暂停问题的答案：每一美元的流动性约为{e5:.0f}倍，因此只要价格停留在区间内，每一美元输给套利的损失也约为{e5:.0f}倍。集中，就是在同一个卖波动率的头寸上加杠杆。',
    "Uniswap's third version, in twenty twenty-one. <bookmark mark='a'/> A provider chooses a price range and supplies liquidity only inside it. Inside, it behaves like a constant-product pool with a larger virtual reserve, holding x of the token, <bookmark mark='b'/> and y of dollars. <bookmark mark='c'/> Outside the range it stops trading and earns nothing: below it, it is all token; above it, all dollars.": "2021年，Uniswap的第三版。<bookmark mark='a'/>提供者选择一个价格区间，只在其中提供流动性。在区间内，它的行为像一个带有更大虚拟储备的恒定乘积池，持有x的代币，<bookmark mark='b'/>以及y的美元。<bookmark mark='c'/>在区间之外它停止交易、什么也赚不到：低于区间时全部是代币，高于区间时全部是美元。",
    'f"A position on ether between {v[\'pa\']:,.0f} and {v[\'pb\']:,.0f} dollars. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Below the range it holds only ether, so its value falls one for one with ether. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Inside, the value bends: concave, short gamma, the pool\'s signature. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Above, it has sold all its ether and holds only dollars: the upside is capped. It is a covered call, written continuously."': "一个以太币价格在{v['pa']:,.0f}到{v['pb']:,.0f}美元之间的头寸。<bookmark mark='a'/>低于区间时，它只持有以太币，所以价值随以太币一比一下跌。<bookmark mark='b'/>在区间内，价值弯曲：凹的、负伽马，这是池子的标志。<bookmark mark='c'/>高于区间时，它已经卖光以太币，只持有美元：上涨收益被封顶。这是一份被持续卖出的备兑看涨期权。",
    'f"How much liquidity a dollar buys at the geometric centre. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> A range from P over w to P times w has efficiency one over one minus w to the minus one half relative to full range at the same price. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> For w equal to one point zero one, about {e1:.0f} times; for one point one, {rows_[3][\'eff\']:.0f}; for two, {rows_[-1][\'eff\']:.1f}. The lower bound is a reciprocal, not a symmetric percentage discount. At equal active liquidity and identical fee allocation, local fee exposure scales too. Real income also depends on volume, competition, time in range and execution costs."': "几何中心处，一美元购买多少流动性？<bookmark mark='a'/> 区间从P除以w到Pw，相对同价全区间的效率为一除以一减w的负二分之一次方。<bookmark mark='b'/> w等于1.01时约 {e1:.0f} 倍；1.1时约 {rows_[3]['eff']:.0f} 倍；2时约 {rows_[-1]['eff']:.1f} 倍。下界是倒数，不是对称百分比折价。活跃流动性与费用分配相同时，局部费用暴露也缩放；真实收入还依赖成交量、竞争、在区间内时间与执行成本。",
    'f"Leaving a range changes the position. Each sample day resets its centre to the first observed ether price. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> For bounds P divided by one point zero one and P times one point zero one, at least one sampled minute lies outside on {100 * r1[\'days_left\']:.0f} percent of days; {100 * r1[\'out_share\']:.0f} percent of sampled observations are outside on average. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> With w equal to one point zero five, these become {100 * r5[\'days_left\']:.0f} percent of days and {100 * r5[\'out_share\']:.1f} percent of sampled time. A daily-mean share gives each day equal weight. Unobserved intraminute exits are missed; these are not continuous barrier-hit probabilities. Re-centering involves trades and costs."': "出界改变仓位。样本每天用第一笔观测的以太币价格重置中心。<bookmark mark='a'/> 上下界为P除以1.01和P乘1.01时，{100 * r1['days_left']:.0f}% 的天数至少有一个分钟观测出界，平均 {100 * r1['out_share']:.0f}% 的采样观测处于区间外。<bookmark mark='b'/> w等于1.05时，对应 {100 * r5['days_left']:.0f}% 的天数和 {100 * r5['out_share']:.1f}% 的采样时间。日均比例使每天等权。未观测的分钟内穿越被遗漏，因此不是连续障碍触碰概率。重置还需要交易及费用。",
    "Concentration changes local curvature. <bookmark mark='a'/> In range, the continuous fee-free loss rate is sigma squared times liquidity times square root of price, divided by four. It vanishes outside the active range in this model. <bookmark mark='b'/> At the geometric centre, divide by the concentrated position's smaller capital value to get the efficiency multiple of the full-range local loss rate. <bookmark mark='c'/> Fee income has the same local multiple only under comparable active-liquidity allocation and volume. Over a path, price location, range exits, competing liquidity and re-centering costs change the result. A local scaling argument does not prove narrow ranges are globally better.": "集中改变局部曲率。<bookmark mark='a'/> 区间内连续无费损失速率是sigma平方乘流动性、乘价格平方根再除以四；模型中区间外为零。<bookmark mark='b'/> 在几何中心，除以集中仓位较小的资本价值，得到相对全区间局部损失的效率倍数。<bookmark mark='c'/> 只有成交量与活跃流动性分配可比，费用收入才有相同局部倍数。整条路径中，价格位置、出界、竞争和重置成本都会改变结果。局部缩放不能证明窄区间总体更好。",
    'f"A contextual-bandit illustration in a chosen simulated world. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Annual volatility is {100 * sig[0]:.0f} or {100 * sig[1]:.0f} percent with a persistent latent regime. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Each day chooses withdrawal or a freshly centred multiplicative range; current action does not control tomorrow\'s regime or observation. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> The state is a bucket of yesterday\'s noisy realized-volatility estimate. <bookmark mark=\'d\'/> Reward is an assumed exogenous daily fee yield times centre efficiency and in-range share, less simulated loss-versus-rebalancing divided by initial daily capital and a reset charge. It is a stylized benchmark-relative reward, not a total executable LP return. The model omits hedge financing, fee competition and realistic transaction costs."': "指定模拟世界中的上下文赌博机。<bookmark mark='a'/> 年波动率为 {100 * sig[0]:.0f}% 或 {100 * sig[1]:.0f}%，隐状态有持续性。<bookmark mark='b'/> 每天选择退出或重新居中的乘法区间；当前行动不控制明天的状态或观测。<bookmark mark='c'/> 状态是昨日含噪已实现波动估计的分桶。<bookmark mark='d'/> 奖励为假设的外生每日费用收益乘中心效率与区间内比例，再减按日初资本归一化的模拟再平衡损失及重置费。这是风格化基准相对奖励，不是可执行LP总收益；对冲融资、费用竞争与真实交易成本未建模。",
    'f"After four thousand simulated days, what it learned, in basis points of capital a day. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> After a calm day, the narrow range is worth about {q_calm:+.0f}; the wider ones much less. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> After a stormy day every range loses, the narrow one most, and withdrawing, worth zero, is best. The middle state almost never occurs, because the two regimes are far apart."': "四千个模拟交易日之后，它学到了什么，以每天资本的基点计。<bookmark mark='a'/>平静的一天之后，窄区间的价值约为{q_calm:+.0f}；更宽的区间少得多。<bookmark mark='b'/>动荡的一天之后，每个区间都亏钱，窄区间亏得最多，而价值为零的撤出最好。中间状态几乎从未出现，因为两种状态相距很远。",
    'f"Evaluation uses two thousand fresh simulated days and common daily random seeds across actions. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> In this chosen run the narrow fixed action averages {narrow:+.0f} basis points of benchmark-relative reward a day. Other fixed actions and withdrawal provide the displayed baselines. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> The learned policy averages {ev[\'learned\'][\'mean_bp\']:+.0f}, versus {ev[\'oracle\'][\'mean_bp\']:+.0f} for a regime-informed action selected using extra Monte Carlo samples. These are one training and evaluation design, with serially dependent regimes, not evidence of live skill or a confidence interval. The oracle has more information and a separate selection budget; it is not an equally informed competitor."': "用两千个新的模拟日评估，各行动共用每日随机种子。<bookmark mark='a'/> 此指定运行中，固定窄区间的基准相对奖励平均每日 {narrow:+.0f} 基点，其他固定行动与退出是所示基线。<bookmark mark='b'/> 学得策略平均 {ev['learned']['mean_bp']:+.0f}，获知状态且另用蒙特卡洛样本选择行动的比较者为 {ev['oracle']['mean_bp']:+.0f}。这是一个训练与评估设计，状态有序列依赖，不是实盘能力证据或置信区间。比较者拥有更多信息和单独选择预算，并非同等信息的竞争者。",
    "What this experiment supports. <bookmark mark='a'/> Fee yield is chosen externally and scales by a simple efficiency factor, rather than arising from traders competing across ranges. <bookmark mark='b'/> Two well-separated regimes and a lagged volatility bucket make the prediction problem easier than a real market; one seeded training run does not quantify training uncertainty. <bookmark mark='c'/> The learner estimates conditional one-step action values, with sample-mean updates and no continuation-value term. This is a contextual bandit, not a general long-horizon liquidity-management policy. Its positive benchmark-relative reward depends on its assumed world and does not establish an investment return.": "这个实验支持什么？<bookmark mark='a'/> 费用收益外生指定，并以简单效率因子缩放，没有让交易者跨区间竞争产生收入。<bookmark mark='b'/> 两个相距很远的状态及滞后波动桶，使预测比现实容易；单个训练种子不能量化训练不确定性。<bookmark mark='c'/> 学习器以样本均值更新条件单步行动价值，没有继续价值项。这是上下文赌博机，不是一般长期流动性管理策略。正的基准相对奖励依赖指定世界，不能确立投资回报。",
    "Pause and predict. A trader buys a hundred thousand dollars of ether from Chapter two's pool and accepts up to one percent of slippage. Someone who can order the block's transactions sees the order first. How much can they take?": '暂停并预测。一位交易者从第2章的池子买入十万美元的以太币，接受最多百分之一的滑点。一个能够安排区块内交易顺序的人先看到了这笔订单。他能拿走多少？',
    'f"Chapter five. In the chosen largest-feasible-front-run calculation, the hundred-thousand-dollar trade at one-percent tolerance produces candidate profit of {r[\'profit\']:,.0f} dollars. The victim\'s token shortfall valued at the initial two-thousand-dollar reference is {r[\'victim_loss\']:,.0f} dollars. Those quantities use different price and counterfactual conventions; their difference is not automatically the pool\'s fee income. We will inspect the transaction ledger and the attack sizing rule before interpreting its output."': "第五章。指定的最大可行抢跑计算中，十万美元交易、1%容忍度的候选利润为 {r['profit']:,.0f} 美元。受害者代币缺口按初始两千美元参考价估值为 {r['victim_loss']:,.0f} 美元。两者价格及反事实口径不同，差额不自动等于池子费用收入。解释输出前，先检查交易账目和规模规则。",
    "How a trade reaches the ledger. <bookmark mark='a'/> A user signs a swap; it waits in a public pool of pending transactions; searchers write bundles of trades around it; builders assemble whole blocks and bid for the right to have them included; the proposer takes the highest bid. <bookmark mark='b'/> Since twenty twenty-two most Ethereum blocks have been built this way, as reported. <bookmark mark='c'/> The value of choosing what goes in a block, and in what order, is called maximal extractable value.": "一笔交易如何到达账本。<bookmark mark='a'/>用户签署一笔兑换；它在待处理交易的公共池里等待；搜索者围绕它编写交易捆绑包；构建者组装整个区块，并为让区块被打包而出价；提议者接受最高出价。<bookmark mark='b'/>据报道，自2022年起，大多数以太坊区块都是这样构建的。<bookmark mark='c'/>选择区块里放什么、按什么顺序放，这件事的价值被称为最大可提取价值。",
    'f"A chosen sandwich on a million-dollar purchase with one-percent tolerance. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The attacker buys first, moving the curve. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> The victim then executes within its minimum-output constraint. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> The attacker sells its token back. The returned candidate profit is {r[\'profit\']:,.0f} dollars, before gas, builder payments and execution competition. Victim shortfall, valued at the initial external reference, is {r[\'victim_loss\']:,.0f} dollars. The bisection maximizes feasible front-run size within a bound; it has not separately proved that this size maximizes profit."': "对一百万美元购买、1%容忍度作指定夹子交易。<bookmark mark='a'/> 攻击者先买，推动曲线。<bookmark mark='b'/> 受害者随后在最小输出约束内执行。<bookmark mark='c'/> 攻击者卖回代币，返回候选利润 {r['profit']:,.0f} 美元，未扣gas、构建者付款与执行竞争。按初始外部参考价估值的受害者缺口为 {r['victim_loss']:,.0f} 美元。二分法只最大化有界可行抢跑规模，未单独证明该规模利润最优。",
    "The sizing constraint. <bookmark mark='a'/> The victim sets a minimum output relative to an unattacked quote; lower tolerance can reduce one opportunity but can also increase failed transactions. <bookmark mark='b'/> This implementation uses bisection to find the largest front-run input that keeps the victim feasible, capped at one hundred times victim input. It is not a general profit optimizer. <bookmark mark='c'/> An attacker can also choose not to attack, so a negative raw candidate is not a rational attack profit. Gas, priority payments, liquidity competition, private routing and other strategies would change the attainable outcome. Tolerance times trade size is only a rough scale, not an exact extraction identity.": "规模约束。<bookmark mark='a'/> 受害者按未受攻击的报价设最小输出；容忍度更低可能减少机会，也可能增加失败交易。<bookmark mark='b'/> 实现用二分法寻找保持受害者可行的最大抢跑输入，上限是受害者输入的一百倍，不是一般利润优化器。<bookmark mark='c'/> 攻击者也能选择不攻击，因此负的原始候选值不是理性攻击利润。Gas、优先付款、竞争流动性、私有路由及其他策略都会改变可达结果。容忍度乘交易量只是粗略尺度，不是精确攫取恒等式。",
    'f"The raw candidates in this chosen pool. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> All four ten-thousand-dollar candidates have negative profits under the largest-feasible sizing rule. That does not prove every alternative attack is unprofitable or that a small trade is safe. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> At one-percent tolerance, the hundred-thousand-dollar candidate returns {r1[\'profit\']:,.0f} dollars. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> At three percent, the million-dollar candidate returns {r3[\'profit\']:,.0f}. These are gross simulator outputs under a fixed curve with input fees outside it. The no-attack option, gas, transaction order uncertainty and competing searchers must be included before an economic decision."': "指定池中的原始候选值。<bookmark mark='a'/> 四个一万美元候选在最大可行规模规则下都为负利润，但不能证明其他攻击都亏损或小交易安全。<bookmark mark='b'/> 1%容忍度时，十万美元候选返回 {r1['profit']:,.0f} 美元。<bookmark mark='c'/> 3%时，一百万美元候选返回 {r3['profit']:,.0f} 美元。这是固定曲线、输入费用记在曲线外的模拟总额。经济决策前必须加入不攻击选项、gas、排序不确定性及竞争搜索者。",
    "Three kinds of extractable value, first catalogued by Philip Daian and coauthors in Flash Boys two point oh, in twenty twenty. <bookmark mark='a'/> Arbitrage, between pools and against centralised exchanges, the largest kind, as studies of on-chain data reported. <bookmark mark='b'/> Liquidations: lending protocols pay a bonus to whoever first repays an under-collateralised loan, and the race for it is a race for position in the block. <bookmark mark='c'/> And sandwiches and just-in-time liquidity: trading around another user's swap, a pure transfer from that user.": "三类可提取价值，最早由Philip Daian和合作者在2020年的《Flash Boys 2.0》中归纳。<bookmark mark='a'/>套利，在池子之间以及池子与中心化交易所之间，据链上数据研究报道，这是最大的一类。<bookmark mark='b'/>清算：借贷协议向最先偿还抵押不足贷款的人支付奖励，争夺它就是争夺区块内的位置。<bookmark mark='c'/>以及三明治攻击和即时流动性：围绕另一位用户的兑换交易，纯粹是从该用户那里的转移。",
    "Keep the ledger and its recipients separate. <bookmark mark='a'/> In this simulator, the pool's own rebalancing-minus-curve gap equals its arbitrage profit plus outside-curve fees, before gas and other participants. This is not a claim that a fee-free reference loss stays unchanged. <bookmark mark='b'/> Searchers, builders and proposers may compete over transaction surplus under their respective arrangements. <bookmark mark='c'/> Bidding can transfer surplus when the auction and competition assumptions support it, but concentration, private information, execution costs and market power change the allocation. Neither a largest-source ranking nor a universal fraction bid away follows from the small simulation.": "把账目与收款者分开。<bookmark mark='a'/> 此模拟中，池子自己的再平衡减曲线价值，等于套利利润加曲线外费用，尚未计gas及其他参与者。这不声称无费参考损失不变。<bookmark mark='b'/> 搜索者、构建者和提议者可能按各自安排竞争交易剩余。<bookmark mark='c'/> 拍卖和竞争假设成立时，竞价可能转移剩余，但集中度、私有信息、执行成本与市场力量会改变分配。小模拟不能推出最大来源排序，也不能给出普遍被竞价转走的比例。",
    "Mechanism choices have limits. <bookmark mark='a'/> Tighter output bounds and private submission can reduce exposure to public-mempool sandwiches, but private intermediaries may still observe or reorder orders and can fail to execute them. <bookmark mark='b'/> Batch settlement and uniform clearing rules can remove some within-batch sequencing advantages for eligible orders, subject to solver, routing and settlement rules. This does not eliminate all forms of extractable value. <bookmark mark='c'/> Auctions of arbitrage rights and dynamic fees aim to reallocate surplus to providers; their net effect depends on competition, implementation and welfare measurement. The small simulator here does not prove a universal guarantee.": "机制选择有边界。<bookmark mark='a'/> 更紧的输出界与私有提交可减少公开内存池夹子暴露，但私有中介仍可能观测、排序或不执行订单。<bookmark mark='b'/> 批量结算和统一清算规则可减少合资格订单在批内的部分排序优势，效果受求解者、路由及结算规则约束，不消除全部可提取价值。<bookmark mark='c'/> 套利权拍卖和动态费用试图把剩余分配给提供者，净效果依赖竞争、实现及福利衡量。这里的小模拟不能证明普遍保证。",
    "Pause and predict. A perpetual future never expires, so nothing forces its price to meet spot at a date. What keeps Bitcoin's perpetual within a few basis points of spot, and who pays for it?": '暂停并预测。永续合约永不到期，所以没有什么在某个日期迫使它的价格与现货相等。是什么让比特币永续合约保持在现货的几个基点之内？谁为此付钱？',
    'f"Chapter six, and the answer to the pause: funding. Every eight hours, holders on one side pay the other, and the payment grows with the perpetual\'s premium over spot. Longs pay when it trades above, which on Bitcoin has been most of the time: about {b[\'annual_pct\']:.0f} percent a year on average since twenty twenty."': "第6章，以及暂停问题的答案：资金费率。每八小时，一方持有者向另一方付款，金额随永续合约相对现货的溢价增加。合约高于现货时由多头付款，而在比特币上大部分时间都是如此：自2020年以来平均每年约{b['annual_pct']:.0f}%。",
    "Funding transfers cash between contract sides. <bookmark mark='a'/> In the sampled eight-hour contract convention, a positive settlement rate makes longs pay shorts on settlement notional. Actual products can use other intervals and caps. <bookmark mark='b'/> A sufficiently positive premium can raise funding, discouraging longs. <bookmark mark='c'/> A negative spot-perpetual premium does not automatically imply negative funding: the clamped interest term can keep it positive near zero. <bookmark mark='d'/> Perpetuals have no scheduled expiry, so linkage to spot depends on funding incentives, arbitrage constraints and contract rules, rather than a guaranteed terminal convergence date.": "资金费在合约双方间转移现金。<bookmark mark='a'/> 样本八小时合约口径下，正费率使多头按结算名义额付给空头；实际产品也可能有其他间隔及上限。<bookmark mark='b'/> 足够正的溢价可能提高资金费，抑制多头。<bookmark mark='c'/> 负的现货永续溢价不自动意味着负资金费：限幅利息项可让零附近费率保持正值。<bookmark mark='d'/> 永续没有预定到期日，与现货的联系依赖资金费激励、套利约束和合约规则，而非保证终点收敛。",
    "The simplified rule in matching eight-hour units. <bookmark mark='a'/> The venue's premium index is a contract-defined index, not simply the difference of hourly closing prices. <bookmark mark='b'/> Funding equals average premium plus the interest-minus-premium term clamped between minus and plus five basis points, under the stated historical convention and before any other caps. <bookmark mark='c'/> If the absolute premium-minus-interest difference is at most five basis points, the rate equals the one-basis-point interest term. Product-specific intervals, index construction, caps and rules must be checked separately. This chosen representation is not a certification of today's venue terms.": "时间单位一致的八小时简化规则。<bookmark mark='a'/> 场所的溢价指数由合约规定，不只是小时收盘价之差。<bookmark mark='b'/> 在所述历史约定及其他上限之前，资金费等于平均溢价，加上利息减溢价在正负五基点内限幅的项。<bookmark mark='c'/> 溢价减利息的绝对值不超过五基点时，费率等于一基点利息。产品间隔、指数构成、上限与规则须另查；指定表示不认证当前场所条款。",
    "A separate continuous-funding model. <bookmark mark='a'/> The long's gains are d F minus kappa times F minus S, times dt. <bookmark mark='b'/> Under a pricing measure, its zero-value gains have zero drift, and spot has drift r minus q. Assume constant coefficients, a linear contract and matching continuous-time units. <bookmark mark='c'/> Try F equal to a constant multiple of S, then equate that multiple times r minus q with kappa times the multiple minus one. <bookmark mark='d'/> This gives F equal to kappa S divided by kappa minus the quantity r minus q, requiring kappa greater than r minus q and a transversality condition to exclude bubbles. This model is distinct from the venue's discrete clamped rule.": "另一个连续资金费模型。<bookmark mark='a'/> 多头收益为dF减去kappa乘F减S再乘dt。<bookmark mark='b'/> 定价测度下，零价值合约收益漂移为零，现货漂移为r减q。假设系数恒定、线性合约且连续时间单位一致。<bookmark mark='c'/> 设F是S的常数倍，将该倍数乘r减q与kappa乘倍数减一相等。<bookmark mark='d'/> 得到F等于kappa S除以kappa减去括号内r减q，要求kappa大于r减q，并以横截条件排除泡沫。它不同于场所的离散限幅规则。",
    "Translate the interest term carefully. <bookmark mark='a'/> One basis point every eight hours gives ten point nine five percent a year by simple notional annualization, using three settlements a day and three hundred sixty-five days. <bookmark mark='b'/> That is neither compounding nor a return on committed strategy capital. <bookmark mark='c'/> Near zero premium, the simplified clamp can preserve this positive rate, so a short receives it at those settlements. Future rates, basis moves, financing, fees, margin and venue losses remain variable; there is no fixed contractual yield from merely buying spot and shorting the perpetual.": "谨慎换算利息项。<bookmark mark='a'/> 每八小时一基点，以每天三次、每年365天简单按名义额年化，是10.95%。<bookmark mark='b'/> 这既不是复利，也不是投入策略资本的收益。<bookmark mark='c'/> 零溢价附近，简化限幅可维持正费率，空头在这些结算点收款。但未来费率、基差变动、融资、费用、保证金和场所损失均可变；买现货并卖永续本身不提供固定契约收益。",
    "Six years of Bitcoin's funding, every ninth settlement, annualised. <bookmark mark='a'/> A dense line at about eleven percent: the interest term, whenever the premium is small. <bookmark mark='b'/> Spikes far above it in the bull market of twenty twenty-one, when leveraged longs paid over a hundred percent a year for their exposure. <bookmark mark='c'/> And spells below zero, in the crashes of twenty twenty-one and twenty twenty-two, when shorts paid.": "比特币六年的资金费率，每九次结算取一次，年化。<bookmark mark='a'/>一条位于约百分之十一处的密集横线：溢价很小时的利息项。<bookmark mark='b'/>2021年牛市中远高于它的尖峰，当时加杠杆的多头为其敞口支付了每年超过百分之一百的费用。<bookmark mark='c'/>以及2021年和2022年崩盘中低于零的时段，那时由空头付款。",
    'f"Describe the frozen sample by year. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Bitcoin\'s mean settlement rate, simply annualized, is {y21[\'annual_pct\']:.0f} percent in twenty twenty-one and {y22[\'annual_pct\']:.0f} in twenty twenty-two; {100 * y22[\'neg\']:.0f} percent of twenty twenty-two settlements are negative. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Across the sampled six years, {100 * b[\'at_base\']:.0f} percent of rates fall within the code\'s tolerance of the one-basis-point base. Mean simple annualized rates are {b[\'annual_pct\']:.0f} percent for Bitcoin and {e[\'annual_pct\']:.0f} for ether. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> The twenty twenty-five Bitcoin mean is {b[\'by_year\'][5][\'annual_pct\']:.0f} percent, with {100 * b[\'by_year\'][5][\'at_base\']:.0f} percent near the base. Changing rates alone do not identify crowding, a policy change or the cause of a premium shift."': "逐年描述冻结样本。<bookmark mark='a'/> 比特币结算平均费率简单年化，2021年为 {y21['annual_pct']:.0f}%，2022年为 {y22['annual_pct']:.0f}%；2022年 {100 * y22['neg']:.0f}% 的结算为负。<bookmark mark='b'/> 六年样本中，{100 * b['at_base']:.0f}% 的费率在代码容差内接近一基点基准。简单年化均值比特币 {b['annual_pct']:.0f}%，以太币 {e['annual_pct']:.0f}%。<bookmark mark='c'/> 2025年比特币均值 {b['by_year'][5]['annual_pct']:.0f}%，接近基准的比例为 {100 * b['by_year'][5]['at_base']:.0f}%。费率变化本身不能识别拥挤、政策调整或溢价变化原因。",
    'f"An observable proxy, not an exact rule replication. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Each selected point pairs a funding settlement with an average of hourly perpetual-to-spot close ratios from the preceding pre-settlement hours. The code permits some missing observations and uses candle-open timestamps for closes. Correlation with funding is {b[\'corr_prem\']:.2f}. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Applying the simplified clamp to that proxy gives correlation {b[\'corr_rule\']:.2f}. The official impact-price premium index, weights, caps and exact observation clocks differ, so correlation does not validate the venue\'s full calculation or prove a causal mechanism. Display filtering removes points outside the plotted window."': "可观测代理，不是精确复现规则。<bookmark mark='a'/> 每个选定点将资金费结算，与此前若干结算前小时的永续现货收盘价比平均值配对。代码允许部分缺失，用蜡烛开盘时戳标记收盘价。与资金费相关为 {b['corr_prem']:.2f}。<bookmark mark='b'/> 将简化限幅用于该代理，相关为 {b['corr_rule']:.2f}。官方冲击价格溢价指数、权重、上限与精确时钟不同，因此相关不验证完整场所计算，也不证明因果机制。显示筛选还移除了绘图区外的点。",
    "Who pays, and why. <bookmark mark='a'/> Positive funding is the price of leverage: what leveraged longs pay for exposure they could not finance in spot, an interest rate set by crypto's own demand for leverage. <bookmark mark='b'/> It is also a gauge of sentiment, high in rallies and negative in crashes, and forced liquidations cluster at its extremes. <bookmark mark='c'/> And it is the running cost that Part two's margin account paid through the crash of March twenty twenty.": "谁付钱，为什么。<bookmark mark='a'/>正的资金费率是杠杆的价格：加杠杆的多头为他们无法在现货中融资获得的敞口所支付的费用，一个由加密市场自身杠杆需求决定的利率。<bookmark mark='b'/>它也是情绪的晴雨表，上涨时高、崩盘时为负，强制平仓集中出现在它的极端值附近。<bookmark mark='c'/>它也是第2部分的保证金账户在2020年3月崩盘中一路支付的持续成本。",
    'f"Pause and predict. In the frozen ether sample, the mean settlement rate has a simple notional annualization of {f[\'ETHUSDT\'][\'annual_pct\']:.0f} percent. A desk proposes to buy one unit of spot and short one linear perpetual unit. Which price exposures cancel in the matched-unit ledger, and which funding, basis, margin, custody and execution risks remain? State the capital denominator before turning any payment into a return."': "暂停预测。冻结以太币样本中，平均结算费率按名义额简单年化为 {f['ETHUSDT']['annual_pct']:.0f}%。交易台拟买一单位现货、卖一单位线性永续。匹配单位账目中哪些共同价格暴露抵消，哪些资金费、基差、保证金、托管与执行风险保留？把付款转成收益前，先明确资本分母。",
    "Chapter seven. The answer to the pause is that funding can turn negative, basis can move, and margin can be exhausted before a spot gain can be transferred. <bookmark mark='a'/> Match one unit of spot against one unit of a linear perpetual. <bookmark mark='b'/> Common price movement largely cancels, but the basis and funding remain. <bookmark mark='c'/> We will work through chosen accounting examples and venue stresses. They demonstrate mechanisms, without reporting a fitted carry strategy, an opened hold-out or an approved trading book.": "第七章。上一题的答案是资金费可变负、基差可变动，现货盈利转移前保证金可能耗尽。<bookmark mark='a'/> 一单位现货匹配一单位线性永续空头。<bookmark mark='b'/> 共同价格变动大体抵消，基差与资金费仍在。<bookmark mark='c'/> 我们推演指定算术与场所压力例子，展示机制，不报告拟合套利策略、已打开留出样本或获准交易账簿。",
    "Write the ledger in dollars for one maintained unit. <bookmark mark='a'/> The spot earns its price change and the short perpetual loses the perpetual's price change. Their sum is minus the change in basis, perpetual minus spot. <bookmark mark='b'/> Add each funding rate times the settlement notional, then subtract commissions, spreads, borrowing and transfer costs. <bookmark mark='c'/> This convention is for a linear contract and a fixed unit quantity. Inverse contracts, changing quantities and collateral denominated in a volatile coin require different ledgers.": "为保持一单位写美元账。<bookmark mark='a'/> 现货赚其价格变化，永续空头亏其价格变化，合计为永续减现货基差变化的负值。<bookmark mark='b'/> 加各资金费率乘结算名义额，再减佣金、价差、借贷与转移成本。<bookmark mark='c'/> 口径限定线性合约和固定单位数。反向合约、数量变化或波动币抵押品都需要不同账目。",
    "Choose spot and perpetual prices of one hundred, and cash collateral equal to one third of the short's notional. <bookmark mark='a'/> Buying the spot uses one hundred dollars; margin uses thirty-three dollars and a third. <bookmark mark='b'/> Total committed capital is therefore one hundred thirty-three and a third before a liquidity buffer. <bookmark mark='c'/> A funding rate of one hundredth of a percent pays one cent on the one-hundred-dollar short, or zero point zero zero seven five percent of committed capital. Margin is committed cash, while a buffer increases the denominator further.": "设现货永续价格均100，现金抵押品等于空头名义额三分之一。<bookmark mark='a'/> 现货花100美元，保证金33又三分之一。<bookmark mark='b'/> 流动性缓冲之前，投入资本133又三分之一。<bookmark mark='c'/> 一万分之一资金费在100美元空头上付一美分，即投入资本的0.0075%。保证金是投入现金，额外缓冲还会提高分母。",
    "Use that same chosen funding settlement. <bookmark mark='a'/> Funding pays one cent, but the perpetual's premium widens from zero to twenty cents. <bookmark mark='b'/> The matched price legs lose twenty cents, regardless of whether both market prices rose or fell together. <bookmark mark='c'/> Net profit before other costs is minus nineteen cents, about minus fourteen basis points of the original capital. The size of a small funding payment does not bound a temporary basis move, and perpetual convergence has no fixed expiry date.": "沿用指定结算。<bookmark mark='a'/> 资金费收一美分，但永续溢价从零扩大到二十美分。<bookmark mark='b'/> 无论两种市场价格共同上升或下降，匹配的价格腿损失二十美分。<bookmark mark='c'/> 其他成本前净损失十九美分，约初始资本负十四基点。小资金费付款不能限制暂时基差变化，永续收敛没有固定到期日。",
    "Now choose a negative funding rate of two hundredths of a percent. <bookmark mark='a'/> On one hundred dollars of perpetual notional, the short pays two cents instead of receiving funding. <bookmark mark='b'/> The long spot does not reimburse that payment. A decision made from a trailing average cannot lock in future rates. <bookmark mark='c'/> Contract caps, settlement intervals, mark conventions and collateral eligibility can also change. Historical average funding is a description of past payments, rather than a contractual yield available at entry.": "现在设负资金费率为0.02%。<bookmark mark='a'/> 对100美元永续名义额，空头付两美分而不是收款。<bookmark mark='b'/> 现货多头不补偿付款，基于过去平均值的决策不能锁定未来费率。<bookmark mark='c'/> 合约上限、结算间隔、标记口径和抵押品资格也会变化。历史平均资金费描述过去付款，不是入场即可取得的契约收益。",
    "Choose a combined entry charge of fifteen basis points of spot notional, and the same again to leave. <bookmark mark='a'/> Entry costs fifteen cents, exit another fifteen, for thirty cents in all. <bookmark mark='b'/> If the one-cent funding payment stayed unchanged and basis did not move, thirty settlements would merely cover those charges. <bookmark mark='c'/> This simple count excludes financing, slippage, transfer delays and the time value of money. A quoted annualized funding number hides both the notional used for costs and the capital needed to earn it.": "设合计入场费为现货名义额十五基点，离场再收同样金额。<bookmark mark='a'/> 入场十五美分，离场十五美分，共三十美分。<bookmark mark='b'/> 若每次一美分付款不变且基差不动，三十次结算才覆盖这些费用。<bookmark mark='c'/> 此计数没有融资、滑点、转移延迟或时间价值。报价年化资金费隐藏了费用名义额及赚取它所需资本。",
    "Choose a rally from one hundred to one hundred fifty on both legs. <bookmark mark='a'/> The spot gains fifty and the perpetual short loses fifty before funding and costs, so the economic price hedge still balances. <bookmark mark='b'/> But fifty of variation loss exceeds the original thirty-three dollars of collateral if the accounts cannot transfer gains promptly. <bookmark mark='c'/> Actual liquidation depends on maintenance margin, marks, collateral value and venue rules, so this example is a cash-flow stress rather than an exact liquidation threshold. A balance-sheet hedge does not supply intraday liquidity.": "设两腿都从100涨至150。<bookmark mark='a'/> 资金费与成本之前，现货赚50、永续空头亏50，经济价格对冲仍平衡。<bookmark mark='b'/> 若账户不能及时转移盈利，50的变动保证金损失却超过原有33美元抵押品。<bookmark mark='c'/> 实际强平取决于维持保证金、标记、抵押品价值与场所规则，因此是现金流压力，不是精确强平阈值。资产负债表对冲不供应日内流动性。",
    "Suppose, as a chosen stress, only the thirty-three dollars of margin is held at a venue and that exposure has zero recovery. <bookmark mark='a'/> The loss is a quarter of the initial one hundred thirty-three dollars of capital. <bookmark mark='b'/> That is an accounting scenario, not a default probability or a forecast of legal recovery. <bookmark mark='c'/> If the spot is also held there, the exposure may be much larger; close-out claims, netting and rehypothecation change it again. Position size needs an exposure map as well as a return estimate.": "作为指定压力，只在场所放33美元保证金，并假设零回收。<bookmark mark='a'/> 损失是初始133美元资本的四分之一。<bookmark mark='b'/> 这是记账情景，不是违约概率或法律回收预测。<bookmark mark='c'/> 若现货也放在那里，暴露可能大得多；平仓请求权、净额及再抵押还会改变结果。仓位大小需要暴露地图，也需要收益估计。",
    "Custody outside the trading venue may reduce one form of venue exposure. <bookmark mark='a'/> It does not automatically let the trader post collateral, recall it instantly or spend an unrealized spot gain. Those rights depend on contracts and operations. <bookmark mark='b'/> Multiple venues can fail together or suspend transfers together, especially when they share banks or a stablecoin. <bookmark mark='c'/> Larger buffers lower some liquidation risks but tie up more capital. A useful stress combines correlated venue loss, adverse basis and delayed collateral movement instead of assuming each happens in isolation.": "场所外托管可能降低一种场所暴露。<bookmark mark='a'/> 它不自动赋予交易者抵押、即时收回或使用未实现现货盈利的能力，权利取决于契约与操作。<bookmark mark='b'/> 多场所可能同时失败或停转移，特别在共用银行或稳定币时。<bookmark mark='c'/> 更大缓冲降低某些强平风险，却占更多资本。有效压力把相关场所损失、不利基差及抵押品转移延迟结合，不假设它们互相独立。",
    "A research protocol begins before seeing evaluation outcomes. <bookmark mark='a'/> Specify the contract, funding clock, capital denominator, fee model, transfer rules, signal information and venue eligibility. <bookmark mark='b'/> Select only on past information, count every configuration, and reserve an untouched evaluation window. Delisting and venue failure belong in the design, with assumptions made visible. <bookmark mark='c'/> An accounting illustration cannot supply historical performance evidence or be described as an independently validated investment strategy.": "研究协议应先于评估结果。<bookmark mark='a'/> 明确合约、资金费时钟、资本分母、费用模型、转移规则、信号信息与场所资格。<bookmark mark='b'/> 只用过去信息选择，计入所有配置，保留未触碰评估窗口。退市与场所失败须纳入设计，假设可见。<bookmark mark='c'/> 记账例子不能提供历史业绩证据，也不能称为独立验证的投资策略。",
    "Why might someone pay the other side? <bookmark mark='a'/> Demand for leveraged directional exposure and limits on arbitrage capital can support positive funding, but that explanation is a hypothesis to test. <bookmark mark='b'/> A matched-unit book still bears basis, funding-reversal, collateral, venue, stablecoin, operational and legal risks. Their relative importance depends on the actual arrangement. <bookmark mark='c'/> A smooth return series can miss a rare loss and cannot by itself justify a large position. Proposed limits should be tested against both cash-flow stresses and enforceable custody rights.": "为什么另一方愿意付费？<bookmark mark='a'/> 杠杆方向需求与套利资本限制可能支持正资金费，但这是待检验假说。<bookmark mark='b'/> 匹配单位仍承担基差、资金费逆转、抵押品、场所、稳定币、操作与法律风险，重要性取决于安排。<bookmark mark='c'/> 平滑收益可能漏掉罕见损失，不能单独证明大仓位合理。拟议限额应以现金流压力及可执行托管权检验。",
    "Pause and predict. Choose a token with eight percent of its reserves temporarily inaccessible at a failed bank, and suppose the remaining ninety-two percent is immediately worth par. <bookmark mark='a'/> Under zero recovery, simple asset accounting gives ninety-two cents per token before any other claims or costs. <bookmark mark='b'/> Now suppose the market quote is eighty-eight cents. <bookmark mark='c'/> Does that quote identify insolvency, illiquidity, or neither? State what you would need to know about redemption access, reserve valuation, the quote currency and the timing before deciding.": "暂停预测。设某代币8%储备暂时困在失败银行，其余92%即时按面值。<bookmark mark='a'/> 其他请求权和费用之前，零回收的简单资产账给每币九十二美分。<bookmark mark='b'/> 市场报价却为八十八美分。<bookmark mark='c'/> 它识别偿付不足、流动性不足，还是两者都不能识别？决策前需知道哪些赎回通道、储备估值、计价货币与时间信息？",
    "Chapter eight. The previous question cannot be decided from a market quote alone. Reserve valuation, other liabilities, redemption rights, the quote currency and access timing all matter. The USDC episode illustrates reserve and redemption uncertainty during a bank failure. Authorities announced protection for Silicon Valley Bank depositors on March twelfth, twenty twenty-three, with access starting Monday the thirteenth. That chronology does not by itself identify every cause of a token's recovery.": '第八章。只看市场报价不能回答上一题。储备估值、其他负债、赎回权、计价货币及通道时序都重要。USDC事件展示银行失败时的储备与赎回不确定性。2023年3月12日，当局宣布保护硅谷银行存款者，13日周一起可取得资金。时间先后本身不能识别代币恢复的全部原因。',
    "Three kinds. <bookmark mark='a'/> Backed by dollars, like tether and USD coin: the issuer holds deposits, bills and repo, and redeems tokens for approved customers. <bookmark mark='b'/> Backed by crypto, like DAI: loans against more than their value in other tokens, liquidated automatically when collateral falls. <bookmark mark='c'/> And backed by a twin: Terra's UST, redeemable for a dollar's worth of a second token that the protocol itself printed.": "三种类型。<bookmark mark='a'/>由美元支持，比如泰达币和USD币：发行方持有存款、国库券和回购，为经过审核的客户赎回代币。<bookmark mark='b'/>由加密资产支持，比如DAI：以价值更高的其他代币作抵押的贷款，抵押品下跌时自动清算。<bookmark mark='c'/>以及由孪生代币支持：Terra的UST，可以兑换价值一美元的第二种代币，而那是协议自己印出来的。",
    "A run mechanism inspired by Diamond and Dybvig. <bookmark mark='a'/> Suppose tokens promise par redemption, subject to their actual legal rights. <bookmark mark='b'/> Choose reserves with liquid fraction ell and a fire-sale haircut d on the rest. <bookmark mark='c'/> Full liquidation then raises ell plus one minus ell times one minus d per token, below par if both illiquidity and the haircut are positive. <bookmark mark='d'/> Sequential service can create incentives to redeem early, but proving a run equilibrium also needs preferences, timing, withdrawal technology and a specified game. This haircut table is accounting, not a solved Diamond-Dybvig model or proof that every illiquid stablecoin must run.": "受Diamond和Dybvig启发的挤兑机制。<bookmark mark='a'/> 设代币承诺按面值赎回，具体受法律权利约束。<bookmark mark='b'/> 指定流动储备比例ell，其余火售折扣d。<bookmark mark='c'/> 全部清算每币筹得ell加一减ell乘一减d；非流动部分与折扣都为正时低于面值。<bookmark mark='d'/> 顺序服务可能激励早赎回，但证明挤兑均衡还需偏好、时序、提取技术与指定博弈。折扣表只是记账，不是已解的Diamond-Dybvig模型，也不证明所有非流动稳定币必然挤兑。",
    "Use the chosen reserve stress table. <bookmark mark='a'/> If all assets are immediately liquid at par and there are no other claims or costs, aggregate reserves cover one dollar per token. That arithmetic does not rule out operational failure or other run motives. <bookmark mark='b'/> With eighty percent liquid and a twenty-percent haircut on the rest, liquidation value is ninety-six cents. It indicates a shortfall under this stress. The last-get field in the unchanged original repeats aggregate liquidation value; it does not solve a last depositor's payoff or establish an equilibrium. Recoveries, access rights and the order of payments need their own model.": "看指定储备压力表。<bookmark mark='a'/> 若全部资产即时按面值变现，无其他索取或费用，储备覆盖每币一美元；算术不排除操作失败或其他挤兑动机。<bookmark mark='b'/> 80%流动、其余折价20%，清算价值九十六美分，表示该压力下短缺。原始计算的last-get字段只是重复总清算价值，不解末位存款者收益，也不确立均衡。回收、权利与付款顺序需要单独模型。",
    'f"USD coin against tether on Binance in March twenty twenty-three. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The frozen observations begin at the same minute as their sample low, {u[\'low\']:.3f}; the earlier decline is therefore unobserved here. This is a venue quote in tether, not a direct dollar redemption price. Circle reported three point three billion dollars at Silicon Valley Bank after its March tenth failure. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> There are {u[\'min_below98\'] / 60:.0f} hours\' worth of sampled minute closes below point nine eight, not necessarily one uninterrupted spell. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> The first later close above point nine nine five appears about {u[\'hours_to_995\']:.0f} hours after the observed low. The official March twelfth depositor announcement is context, not an identified causal estimate."': "2023年3月Binance上USDC对USDT。<bookmark mark='a'/> 冻结观测起点恰是样本低点 {u['low']:.3f}，因此更早下跌未被观察。这是USDT场所报价，不是直接美元赎回价。3月10日硅谷银行失败后，Circle披露有33亿美元在该行。<bookmark mark='b'/> 低于0.98的分钟收盘价合计约 {u['min_below98'] / 60:.0f} 小时，不一定连续。<bookmark mark='c'/> 低点后首个超过0.995的收盘约在 {u['hours_to_995']:.0f} 小时后。3月12日官方存款者公告是背景，不是已识别因果估计。",
    'f"Compare a chosen reserve calculation with the observed quote. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Treat eight percent as bank exposure and assume every other reserve is worth par, without other claims or costs. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Even zero recovery on that exposure then leaves ninety-two cents per token in the scenario. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> The sample quote of {u[\'low\']:.2f} tether is lower, but it does not prove a liquidity-only explanation or establish ninety-two cents as a universal lower bound. Quote-currency risk, inaccessible reserves, uncertainty, trading constraints and legal redemption rights can all matter. Reserve accounting and immediate market execution are different objects."': "把指定储备算术与报价比较。<bookmark mark='a'/> 设银行暴露8%，其他储备都按面值，没有额外索取或费用。<bookmark mark='b'/> 即使该暴露零回收，情景中每币仍有九十二美分。<bookmark mark='c'/> 样本报价 {u['low']:.2f} USDT更低，却不证明纯流动性解释，也不确立普遍九十二美分下界。计价币风险、不可访问储备、不确定性、交易约束与法律赎回权都可能重要。储备记账与即时市场执行不同。",
    "What normally holds the peg is Part thirty-eight's ETF arbitrage. <bookmark mark='a'/> Below a dollar, buy tokens and redeem them with the issuer. <bookmark mark='b'/> Above, deposit dollars, mint and sell. <bookmark mark='c'/> But only approved customers can, and only when banks are open; as Richard Lyons and Ganesh Viswanath-Natraj showed, the peg is only as tight as access to that window.": "平时维持锚定的是第38部分的ETF套利。<bookmark mark='a'/>低于一美元时，买入代币，向发行方赎回。<bookmark mark='b'/>高于一美元时，存入美元，铸造并卖出。<bookmark mark='c'/>但只有经过审核的客户才能这样做，而且只能在银行营业时间；正如Richard Lyons和Ganesh Viswanath-Natraj所示，锚定的紧密程度取决于进入这个窗口的通道。",
    "Terra, in May twenty twenty-two. <bookmark mark='a'/> The protocol swapped one UST for a dollar's worth of newly minted LUNA, its twin. <bookmark mark='b'/> Below a dollar, arbitrageurs burn UST, receive LUNA, and sell it. <bookmark mark='c'/> That floods the market with LUNA and pushes its price down, <bookmark mark='d'/> so each further redemption mints even more LUNA. The defence feeds on itself. Demand for UST rested largely on a lending protocol, Anchor, that paid close to twenty percent on deposits, as reported.": "2022年5月的Terra。<bookmark mark='a'/>协议把一个UST兑换成价值一美元的新铸LUNA，它的孪生代币。<bookmark mark='b'/>低于一美元时，套利者销毁UST、收到LUNA并卖出。<bookmark mark='c'/>这让LUNA涌入市场并压低它的价格，<bookmark mark='d'/>于是每一次新的赎回都会铸造出更多LUNA。防御在自我吞噬。据报道，对UST的需求主要依赖一个借贷协议Anchor，它为存款支付接近百分之二十的利息。",
    'f"On Binance, hour by hour. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> UST began the month at a dollar and lost the peg on the ninth; by the time trading stopped it was near {ut[\'last\']:.2f}. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> LUNA, at about {lu[\'first\']:.0f} dollars on the first, fell by more than six orders of magnitude in a week, as the redemptions printed it by the trillion. Tens of billions of dollars of market value were gone, as reported."': "币安上，逐小时。<bookmark mark='a'/>UST月初为一美元，9日脱锚；到交易停止时，它接近{ut['last']:.2f}。<bookmark mark='b'/>LUNA在1日约为{lu['first']:.0f}美元，一周内下跌了六个数量级以上，因为赎回以万亿为单位印出了它。据报道，数百亿美元的市值灰飞烟灭。",
    "Three lessons. <bookmark mark='a'/> A coin backed by a token its own system prints is backed by confidence, and when confidence goes, both go together. <bookmark mark='b'/> Contagion: lenders exposed to Terra and to each other failed through the summer, as reported, and FTX followed in November, Part forty-one's spiral in miniature. <bookmark mark='c'/> And the law: Terraform Labs and its founder were found liable for fraud by an American jury in twenty twenty-four. The December twenty twenty-four SEC release records that civil outcome; civil findings and criminal proceedings are separate.": "三点教训。<bookmark mark='a'/> 若代币靠自身体系发行的另一代币支持，其支撑依赖对该体系的信心；信心消失时，两者可能一起下跌。<bookmark mark='b'/> 传染方面，据当时报导，对Terra以及彼此有暴露的放贷机构在夏季陆续倒闭，FTX随后在十一月倒闭，是第四十一部分螺旋的缩影。<bookmark mark='c'/> 法律方面，Terraform Labs及创始人在二零二四年被美国陪审团认定承担欺诈民事责任。同年十二月SEC新闻稿记录了这一民事结果；民事认定与刑事程序应分开。",
    "Historical legal milestones need dates and scope. <bookmark mark='a'/> The European Union's MiCA rules for asset-referenced and e-money tokens generally began applying on June thirtieth, twenty twenty-four, with other provisions and transitions on different schedules. <bookmark mark='b'/> The United States GENIUS Act became Public Law one nineteen twenty-seven on July eighteenth, twenty twenty-five. It specifies permitted reserve assets and an implementation framework; enactment is distinct from its conditional effective date and later rules. <bookmark mark='c'/> These historical sources do not certify current compliance, insurance or instantaneous liquidity. A liquid asset can still be inaccessible during a redemption or banking interruption.": "历史法律节点要有日期和范围。<bookmark mark='a'/> 欧盟MiCA的资产参考代币与电子货币代币条款一般自2024年6月30日适用，其他条款和过渡有不同日程。<bookmark mark='b'/> 美国GENIUS法案于2025年7月18日成为119-27号公法，规定合资格储备资产及实施框架；成法不同于条件生效日与后续规则。<bookmark mark='c'/> 这些历史资料不认证当前合规、保险或即时流动性。赎回和银行中断时，即使资产流动，也可能无法访问。",
    'Pause and predict. In early twenty eighteen, Bitcoin cost tens of percent more in South Korea than in the United States, for weeks. Why did arbitrageurs not close the gap?': '暂停并预测。2018年初，比特币在韩国比在美国贵出百分之几十，持续了好几周。为什么套利者没有消除这个差距？',
    "Chapter nine, and the answer to the pause: capital controls. An arbitrageur must buy in one country and sell in the other, and then move the money back; Korea's limits on moving won abroad, and on foreign accounts at its exchanges, made the second leg slow and costly. A market without a closing bell can still have borders.": '第9章，以及暂停问题的答案：资本管制。套利者必须在一个国家买入、在另一个国家卖出，然后把钱转回来；韩国对韩元汇出和外国人在其交易所开户的限制，让第二条腿既慢又贵。一个没有收盘铃的市场，仍然可以有国界。',
    "Igor Makarov and Antoinette Schoar's study of crypto arbitrage. <bookmark mark='a'/> Within a country, exchanges in the same currency stayed close, because coins and cash move easily between them. <bookmark mark='b'/> Across borders, gaps were large and lasting: premiums in Korea that peaked above forty percent in early twenty eighteen. <bookmark mark='c'/> And the gaps rose together when buying pressure rose. What was scarce was arbitrage capital that could cross the border, not information.": "Igor Makarov和Antoinette Schoar对加密套利的研究。<bookmark mark='a'/>在同一个国家内，以同一种货币交易的交易所价格很接近，因为币和现金在它们之间很容易转移。<bookmark mark='b'/>跨越国界，差距大而持久：韩国的溢价在2018年初一度超过百分之四十。<bookmark mark='c'/>而且买入压力上升时，这些差距一起扩大。稀缺的是能够跨越国界的套利资本，而不是信息。",
    "Where the price is made. <bookmark mark='a'/> Part thirty-five's information shares found Bitcoin's price discovered mostly on the perpetual, where leverage is cheapest. <bookmark mark='b'/> Pools on chain rarely lead; Chapter three's arbitrageurs carry the price to them. <bookmark mark='c'/> And on weekends crypto keeps trading while Chicago's futures and the funds are closed, so the listed products open on Monday wherever crypto went.": "价格在哪里形成。<bookmark mark='a'/>第35部分的信息份额发现，比特币的价格主要在永续合约上被发现，那里的杠杆最便宜。<bookmark mark='b'/>链上的池子很少领先；第3章的套利者把价格带给它们。<bookmark mark='c'/>周末加密市场照常交易，而芝加哥的期货和基金都休市，所以挂牌产品在星期一开盘时，会跳到加密市场已经去到的地方。",
    "Before the funds, a trust. <bookmark mark='a'/> Grayscale's Bitcoin trust created shares but never redeemed them. <bookmark mark='b'/> Without Part thirty-eight's creation and redemption, nothing tied its price to the bitcoin it held: it traded at premiums for years, and at a discount of close to half its value in twenty twenty-two, as reported. <bookmark mark='c'/> All the while its holders paid a fee of two percent a year on the full value.": "在基金之前，是一只信托。<bookmark mark='a'/>灰度的比特币信托只创设份额，从不赎回。<bookmark mark='b'/>没有第38部分的申购和赎回，就没有什么把它的价格与它持有的比特币绑在一起：据报道，它多年溢价交易，在2022年则以接近一半的价值折价交易。<bookmark mark='c'/>与此同时，持有人一直按全部价值每年支付百分之二的费用。",
    'f"Read exactly what was computed. GBTC\'s market close divided by Binance\'s Bitcoin daily close is normalized to one near the end of twenty twenty-two. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The ratio rose during twenty twenty-three; the August court decision and January approval are dated context. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Near January tenth, twenty twenty-four, the ratio is {100 * gb[\'rise\']:.0f} percent above that chosen base. This is not a measured NAV discount: the calculation omits bitcoin entitlement per share, fee erosion and synchronized valuation clocks. The labels do not identify the court decision\'s causal price effect. Conversion changed redemption access, while fees can change bitcoin per share over time."': "严格按计算解读。GBTC市场收盘价除以Binance比特币日收盘价，在2022年末附近归一为一。<bookmark mark='a'/> 比值2023年上升，8月法院决定与1月批准是日期背景。<bookmark mark='b'/> 2024年1月10日附近，比选定基准高 {100 * gb['rise']:.0f}%。它不是净值折价，因为没有每份比特币权利、费用侵蚀或同步估值时钟。标签不识别判决的因果价格效应；转换改变赎回通道，费用也会随时间改变每份比特币量。",
    'f"Spot Bitcoin exchange-traded products began United States trading in January twenty twenty-four after the January tenth approval order. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Approval and first trading are different dates, and not every approved product launched together. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> For IBIT, daily volume times closing price is {ib[\'first_day_bn\']:.1f} billion dollars on the first observed day. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Its mean is {ib[\'mean_bn\']:.1f} billion over the selected twenty twenty-four observations. This is a close-times-volume turnover proxy, not exact traded dollar value or fund inflow. <bookmark mark=\'d\'/> Creation and redemption terms, cash funding, costs and current eligibility must be checked against actual product documents; listing approval is not investment approval."': "美国现货比特币交易所交易产品在2024年1月10日批准令之后开始交易。<bookmark mark='a'/> 批准与首日交易不同，并非每个获批产品一起上线。<bookmark mark='b'/> IBIT首个观测日，日成交量乘收盘价为 {ib['first_day_bn']:.1f} 十亿美元。<bookmark mark='c'/> 选定2024年观测平均 {ib['mean_bn']:.1f} 十亿美元。这是收盘价乘量的周转代理，不是精确成交金额或基金流入。<bookmark mark='d'/> 申赎条款、现金融资、成本与当前资格要查产品文件；上市批准不是投资批准。",
    "Research on token returns. <bookmark mark='a'/> Liu, Tsyvinski and Wu study crypto market, size and momentum factors in their chosen samples; factor fit is an empirical result rather than a universal pricing law. <bookmark mark='b'/> Liu and Tsyvinski report distinctive exposures, momentum and attention relationships for their period. Market composition, survivorship, trading costs and subsequent structural change limit extrapolation. <bookmark mark='c'/> A predictive model from another part is not independent validation of this desk. We do not use sealed strategy outcomes here, and descriptive cross-sectional patterns do not establish implementable net alpha or justify an additional market trial.": "代币收益研究。<bookmark mark='a'/> Liu、Tsyvinski和Wu在选定样本研究市场、规模与动量因子；因子拟合是经验结果，不是普遍定价规律。<bookmark mark='b'/> Liu与Tsyvinski报告其时期的特殊暴露、动量和注意力关系；市场构成、存活偏差、成本及后续结构变化限制外推。<bookmark mark='c'/> 另一部分的预测模型不独立验证此交易台。这里不使用封存策略结果，横截面描述也不确立可实现净alpha或支持新增市场试验。",
    "Firms, from the public record. <bookmark mark='a'/> In a settled order of December twenty twenty-four, the SEC found that Tai Mo Shan, an affiliate of Jump Trading, had bought UST in May twenty twenty-one in a way that misled investors about the peg's mechanism; it agreed to pay about a hundred and twenty-three million dollars without admitting or denying the findings. <bookmark mark='b'/> For token market making, examine compensation, options, inventory and conflicts. Quoted volume alone does not establish independent executable liquidity. <bookmark mark='c'/> A venue can combine custody, execution, collateral and clearing. Map legal claims and operational dependencies before calling these functions diversified.": "从公开记录看机构。<bookmark mark='a'/> 二零二四年十二月的和解命令中，SEC认定Jump Trading关联企业Tai Mo Shan在二零二一年五月购买UST的方式，使投资者误解了锚定机制。该公司同意支付约一亿二千三百万美元，既不承认也不否认相关认定。<bookmark mark='b'/> 代币做市要检查报酬、期权、库存与利益冲突。报价成交量本身不能证明存在独立且可执行的流动性。<bookmark mark='c'/> 同一场所可结合托管、执行、抵押品与清算。在称这些功能已分散之前，先画出法律请求权与操作依赖。",
    "Pause and predict. The House opens a digital-assets desk to run Chapter seven's carry book and to provide liquidity in pools. Which three limits should its rule set before the first trade?": '暂停并预测。本系列公司开设一个数字资产交易台，运行第7章的期现套利组合，并在池子里提供流动性。在第一笔交易之前，它的规则应设定哪三个限额？',
    "The answer to the pause. <bookmark mark='a'/> First, venues: a cap on the collateral any one exchange holds, because the carry book's real tail is the venue. <bookmark mark='b'/> Second, dollars: a cap on any one stablecoin, because issuer, reserve and redemption risks can concentrate in the cash leg. <bookmark mark='c'/> Third, pools: provide liquidity only where fees beat the measured loss to arbitrage, with the token exposure hedged.": "暂停题的答案。<bookmark mark='a'/> 第一，场所：限制任何一家交易所持有的抵押品，因为套利组合的重要尾部风险来自场所。<bookmark mark='b'/> 第二，现金腿：限制单一稳定币，因为发行人、储备与赎回风险可能集中在现金腿。<bookmark mark='c'/> 第三，池子：只有费用超过所测得的套利损失、且代币暴露得到对冲时，才考虑提供流动性。",
    'Chapter ten. The proposed thirty-ninth rule is to measure the risks that a return series may omit. A digital-assets desk needs separate market, collateral, contract, custody and redemption controls. The examples in this lecture motivate a research checklist, rather than certify a strategy or approve capital.': '第十章。拟议第三十九条规则是衡量收益序列可能遗漏的风险。数字资产交易台需要分别控制市场、抵押品、合约、托管与赎回。本讲例子形成研究清单，不认证策略或批准资本。',
    "Read the sheet with its units. <bookmark mark='a'/> The ether loss number is a sum normalized by each step's pool value; realized variance over eight is its small-step comparison, not an independent estimate of a fixed-capital return. The fee simulation uses a separate fee-free denominator. Concentrated-range efficiency is a local centre comparison, while sampled out-of-range days use minute observations. Funding is a simple annualization of settlement rates, not a financed strategy return. The venue loss is a chosen zero-recovery accounting stress. The USDC quote is against tether on one venue. None of these figures alone establishes a deployable desk.": "按单位读表。<bookmark mark='a'/> 以太币损失是各步按池价值归一化之和；已实现方差除以八是小步长比较，不是独立估计固定资本收益。费用模拟使用单独无费分母。集中效率是局部中心比较，出界天数取分钟观测。资金费是结算费率简单年化，不是融资策略收益。场所损失为指定零回收压力，USDC报价来自一个场所且以USDT计价。没有一个数字单独确立可部署交易台。",
    "Proposed venue controls. <bookmark mark='a'/> Custody outside a trading venue may reduce direct exposure, but posting and recalling collateral require an enforceable agreement and tested operations. Keeping margin close to a minimum can increase liquidation risk. <bookmark mark='b'/> Set exposure caps and liquidity buffers across correlated venues, banks and stablecoins; a successful small withdrawal does not prove solvency or guarantee future access. <bookmark mark='c'/> Review ownership, liabilities, audits, legal segregation, netting and recovery rights. A proof of reserves without liabilities is insufficient evidence of solvency.": "拟议场所控制。<bookmark mark='a'/> 场所外托管可能降低直接暴露，但抵押和收回需要可执行协议与测试操作。保证金贴近最低值会增加强平风险。<bookmark mark='b'/> 对相关场所、银行、稳定币设暴露上限和流动性缓冲；小额提款成功不证明偿付能力或未来通道。<bookmark mark='c'/> 审查所有权、负债、审计、法律隔离、净额与回收权。没有负债的储备证明不足以证明偿付能力。",
    "Contracts. <bookmark mark='a'/> On chain, the code is the counterparty, and exploits of bridges and protocols have taken hundreds of millions of dollars at a time, as reported. <bookmark mark='b'/> The House uses only audited contracts with long records and much at stake, and caps exposure to each. <bookmark mark='c'/> And it checks what price each protocol reads, because a manipulable oracle can be drained with a flash loan.": "合约。<bookmark mark='a'/>在链上，代码就是交易对手；据报道，跨链桥和协议的漏洞攻击一次就能卷走数亿美元。<bookmark mark='b'/>本系列公司只使用经过审计、记录很长、利害攸关的合约，并对每一个设敞口上限。<bookmark mark='c'/>它还检查每个协议读取的是什么价格，因为可被操纵的预言机可以用闪电贷掏空。",
    "Operations. <bookmark mark='a'/> No single person can move funds: several signers, or keys split by multi-party computation, with limits per transaction. <bookmark mark='b'/> The market never closes, so neither do the limits: automated checks and an on-call trader every hour of the week. <bookmark mark='c'/> And Part thirty-four's compliance applies on chain: sanctions screening of addresses, and a record of every transaction.": "运营。<bookmark mark='a'/>任何单个人都不能转移资金：多个签名人，或用多方计算拆分的密钥，并有单笔交易限额。<bookmark mark='b'/>市场永不收盘，所以限额也永不休息：自动检查，以及一周每个小时都有值班交易员。<bookmark mark='c'/>第34部分的合规同样适用于链上：对地址进行制裁筛查，并记录每一笔交易。",
    "Chapter three's simulator at its core. In each block, if the pool's price net of the fee is above the market, an arbitrageur sells it the token until the band's edge; if below, buys; and inside the band, nothing happens.": '第3章模拟器的核心。在每个区块里，如果池子扣除手续费后的价格高于市场，套利者就把代币卖给它，直到区间边缘；如果低于市场，就买入；在区间之内，什么也不发生。',
    'Three source lines with distinct scope. The first is the exact fee-free one-step constant-product gap. The second is the continuous local loss rate under its price and regularity assumptions. The third uses proportional fee in a Poisson-block trade-probability approximation; the stationary log-band expression uses minus log one minus fee instead. These unchanged library lines are shown as implementation excerpts, not interchangeable universal formulas.': '三行源代码口径不同。第一行是精确无费常数乘积单步缺口。第二行是在价格与正则性假设下的连续局部损失速率。第三行在泊松出块交易概率近似中使用比例费用；平稳对数费用带公式则用负log一减费率。这些库代码片段不是可互换的普遍公式。',
    "Chapter five's attack: the attacker's purchase, the victim's, and the attacker's sale; the front-run is the largest that keeps the victim within its limit.": '第5章的攻击：攻击者的买入、受害者的买入、攻击者的卖出；抢先交易的规模是让受害者仍在限度之内的最大值。',
    "And Chapter six: Binance's funding rule, the premium plus a clamped interest term, and the perpetual's no-arbitrage multiple of spot.": '还有第6章：币安的资金费率规则，即溢价加上一个被限制的利息项，以及永续合约相对现货的无套利倍数。',
    "The tools this part adds. <bookmark mark='a'/> Pools, what pools lose, and ordering and perpetuals. <bookmark mark='b'/> And the thirty-ninth rule. The House values every pool position against rebalancing, at the frequency of arbitrage and with fat tails. It caps the collateral at any one venue and the exposure to any one stablecoin. And it sizes carry by the loss of a venue, not by its Sharpe ratio.": "这一部分新增的工具。<bookmark mark='a'/>池子、池子亏掉了什么，以及交易顺序和永续合约。<bookmark mark='b'/>还有第39条规则。本系列公司以再平衡为基准评估每一个池子头寸，按套利的频率、并考虑肥尾。它对任何一家交易场所的抵押品和任何一种稳定币的敞口设上限。它按失去一个交易场所的损失来确定期现套利的规模，而不是按它的夏普比率。",
    "The rule against three cases. <bookmark mark='a'/> A pool advertised by its fee yield: ask for its loss to arbitrage, because fees without it are half the account. <bookmark mark='b'/> A basis fund with a Sharpe ratio of four: ask where the collateral sits, in which stablecoin, and what one venue's failure would cost. <bookmark mark='c'/> A stablecoin paying twenty percent: ask what backs it and who pays the yield.": "用三个案例检验这条规则。<bookmark mark='a'/>一个以手续费收益率做广告的池子：问它输给套利的损失，因为只有手续费没有损失，账只算了一半。<bookmark mark='b'/>一只夏普比率为四的基差基金：问抵押品放在哪里、用的是哪种稳定币，以及一家交易场所倒闭会损失多少。<bookmark mark='c'/>一枚支付百分之二十的稳定币：问它由什么支持，以及谁在支付这份收益。",
    "For the researcher. Chapter three measured the loss of a pool to arbitrageurs. This chapter proves the formula behind it, due to Jason Milionis, Ciamac Moallemi, Tim Roughgarden and Anthony Lee Zhang; derives the exact discrete version; proves how fees and block times decide what arbitrageurs keep; and checks each result by simulation and on ether's real prices.": '写给研究者。第3章测量了池子输给套利者的损失。本章证明它背后的公式，来自Jason Milionis、Ciamac Moallemi、Tim Roughgarden和Anthony Lee Zhang；推导精确的离散版本；证明手续费和区块时间如何决定套利者留下多少；并用模拟和以太币的真实价格检验每一个结果。',
    "Specify the model before the proof. <bookmark mark='a'/> Let price be a positive continuous semimartingale. The displayed driftless diffusion is a useful special case; a drift term would cancel from the loss identity too. Assume predictable locally integrable holdings and sufficient local smoothness of pool value. <bookmark mark='b'/> With instantaneous fee-free arbitrage, the pool chooses the minimum external-price value on its feasible curve, with a well-defined minimizing holding. <bookmark mark='c'/> Its marked value is price times token holdings plus numeraire holdings. <bookmark mark='d'/> Start the self-financing rebalancing portfolio at exactly the same value and let its gains be token holdings times the price increment. Expectation statements require additional martingale and integrability conditions.": "证明前先给模型。<bookmark mark='a'/> 价格为正连续半鞅。图上的无漂移扩散是特例；加入漂移也会在损失恒等式中抵消。假设持仓可预测、局部可积，池价值有足够局部光滑性。<bookmark mark='b'/> 即时无费套利使池子在可行曲线上选择外部价格计价最小点，且最优持仓有明确定义。<bookmark mark='c'/> 标记价值为价格乘代币量加计价币量。<bookmark mark='d'/> 自融资再平衡组合从完全相同价值出发，其收益为代币量乘价格增量。期望结论还需真鞅与可积条件。",
    "Lemma one uses the pool's value function. <bookmark mark='a'/> It is the infimum over a price-independent feasible set of affine functions of the external price. <bookmark mark='b'/> An infimum of affine functions is concave. <bookmark mark='c'/> If the minimizing token holding is unique and the value function differentiable, the envelope theorem gives V prime equal to that holding. Without uniqueness, supergradients replace a single derivative and the smooth proof needs modification. The geometry explains the sign; it does not by itself guarantee all the regularity needed for Itô's formula.": "引理一从价值函数出发。<bookmark mark='a'/> 它是价格独立可行集上、外部价格仿射函数的下确界。<bookmark mark='b'/> 仿射函数下确界是凹函数。<bookmark mark='c'/> 若最小化代币持仓唯一且价值可微，包络定理给V的一阶导数等于持仓。没有唯一性时，用超梯度代替单一导数，光滑证明需修改。几何解释符号，但不自动保证Itô公式所需全部正则性。",
    "Lemma two. <bookmark mark='a'/> The second derivative is the slope of the holdings, and concavity makes it negative or zero. <bookmark mark='b'/> A pool sells the token as its price rises and buys as it falls: it always trades against the move. That is the whole source of the loss.": "引理二。<bookmark mark='a'/>二阶导数就是持仓的斜率，凹性使它小于或等于零。<bookmark mark='b'/>价格上涨时池子卖出代币，下跌时买入：它总是逆着走势交易。这就是损失的全部来源。",
    "The pathwise identity. <bookmark mark='a'/> With common initial wealth, smooth concave pool value and instantaneous fee-free arbitrage, rebalancing minus pool value equals minus one half the integral of V double prime against the continuous price's quadratic variation. For the displayed diffusion that is the integral of sigma squared P squared over two times the absolute derivative of token holdings. <bookmark mark='b'/> It is nondecreasing under these assumptions. It depends on the path and its price levels, not only the endpoint. Jumps introduce additional concavity gaps, and fee bands use different holdings; neither is covered by simply reusing the smooth continuous rate.": "逐路径恒等式。<bookmark mark='a'/> 共同初始财富、光滑凹价值及即时无费套利下，再平衡减池价值，等于负二分之一乘V二阶导数对连续价格二次变差的积分。图示扩散下，它是sigma平方、P平方除以二，再乘代币持仓导数绝对值的时间积分。<bookmark mark='b'/> 在这些假设下过程单调不减。它依赖路径及价格水平，而不只依赖终点。跳跃另有凹性差额，费用带使用不同持仓；直接套用光滑连续速率不能覆盖两者。",
    "Apply Itô's formula, locally if necessary. <bookmark mark='a'/> The pool change is V prime times d P plus one half V double prime times d quadratic variation of P. <bookmark mark='b'/> Replace V prime by token holdings. Concavity makes V double prime nonpositive wherever it exists. <bookmark mark='c'/> The benchmark's gains are those same holdings times d P, so their entire stochastic integral cancels, including any finite-variation drift. Integrate from a common initial value. What remains is a nonnegative finite-variation process. It need not be deterministic; its coefficient can depend on the realized price path. A true-martingale expectation claim needs integrability beyond this local identity.": "必要时局部应用Itô公式。<bookmark mark='a'/> 池变化为V一阶导数乘dP，加二分之一V二阶导数乘P二次变差。<bookmark mark='b'/> 一阶导数换成代币量，凹性使存在处的二阶导数非正。<bookmark mark='c'/> 基准收益恰为相同代币量乘dP，因此整个随机积分抵消，包括有限变差漂移。从共同初值积分，剩下非负有限变差过程。它不必确定，系数可依赖实现价格路径。真鞅期望结论需要局部恒等式之外的可积性。",
    "Two local rates. <bookmark mark='a'/> Constant-product value is twice square root of k P, whose second derivative gives sigma squared V over eight. <bookmark mark='b'/> A concentrated position gives sigma squared L square root of P over four while strictly in range, and zero outside. Its first derivative is continuous at the boundaries; a piecewise smooth Itô formula applies without an extra local-time term from a derivative jump. <bookmark mark='c'/> At fifty percent annual volatility the instantaneous normalized full-range loss rate is three point one two five percent per year. That is a rate relative to current value, not the realized annual return or a fee-inclusive strategy forecast.": "两个局部速率。<bookmark mark='a'/> 常数乘积价值为二乘kP的平方根，二阶导数给sigma平方V除以八。<bookmark mark='b'/> 集中仓位在严格区间内给sigma平方L根号P除以四，区间外为零。一阶导数在边界连续，分段光滑Itô可用，没有导数跳跃带来的额外局部时项。<bookmark mark='c'/> 年波动率50%时，全区间即时归一化速率为每年3.125%。这是相对当前价值的速率，不是实际年收益或含费策略预测。",
    "An exact discrete accounting check. <bookmark mark='a'/> Start a fee-free constant-product pool at external price P zero. The benchmark holds its initial token quantity through one price step and starts at the same value. Subtract the pool's value change from that holding's gains. <bookmark mark='b'/> The result is starting pool value over two times square root of the price ratio minus one, squared, for any positive ratio. <bookmark mark='c'/> For a conditionally martingale lognormal ratio with variance parameter sigma squared delta t, its conditional expectation is starting value times one minus exp of minus sigma squared delta t over eight. <bookmark mark='d'/> Divide by delta t and shrink the step to obtain the local continuous rate. A finite price doubling alone does not specify the variance parameter.": "精确离散记账检查。<bookmark mark='a'/> 无费常数乘积池从外部价格P零开始，基准以共同价值出发，在单步内保持初始代币量。用持仓收益减池价值变化。<bookmark mark='b'/> 任意正价格比，结果为初始池价值一半乘根号价格比减一的平方。<bookmark mark='c'/> 若条件价格比为鞅型对数正态，方差参数sigma平方delta t，条件期望是初始价值乘一减指数负sigma平方delta t除以八。<bookmark mark='d'/> 除以delta t并缩小步长，得到局部连续速率。一次价格翻倍本身不指定方差参数。",
    'f"Check one: simulation. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Four hundred thousand steps of a lognormal price, and a pool traded to the market at every step. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> The exact identity, summed step by step, matches the simulated loss to rounding. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> And the continuous formula is within {100 * abs(r[\'ratio\'] - 1):.2f} percent."': "检验一：模拟。<bookmark mark='a'/>四十万步对数正态价格，池子每一步都被交易到市场价格。<bookmark mark='b'/>逐步累加的精确恒等式与模拟的损失在舍入误差内相等。<bookmark mark='c'/>连续公式的误差在{100 * abs(r['ratio'] - 1):.2f}%以内。",
    "A different check examines one-step moments. The unchanged calculation resets its generator and rescales the same four million standard-normal draws for each variance, while keeping the number of draws fixed. <bookmark mark='a'/> Step sigma falls from one to one eighth. The Monte Carlo column estimates the expected normalized one-step loss divided by sigma squared over eight. <bookmark mark='b'/> The closed expectation ratio is one minus exp of minus sigma squared over eight, divided by sigma squared over eight, approaching one as step variance shrinks. <bookmark mark='c'/> This is a moment comparison with sampling error. It is not a nested Brownian path, a fixed-horizon refinement experiment, or proof of pathwise convergence.": "另一项检查考察单步矩。原始计算每组重置发生器，重缩放相同四百万个标准正态数，抽样数保持不变。<bookmark mark='a'/> 单步sigma由一降到八分之一，蒙特卡洛列估计归一化单步期望损失除以sigma平方除以八。<bookmark mark='b'/> 闭式期望比率为一减指数负sigma平方除以八，再除以sigma平方除以八；单步方差缩小时趋于一。<bookmark mark='c'/> 这是含抽样误差的矩比较，不是嵌套布朗路径、固定期限网格细化，也不证明逐路径收敛。",
    'f"Check two: a concentrated position. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> A range from sixty to a hundred and sixty along the same kind of path, in range {100 * v[\'in_range\']:.0f} percent of the time. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> The simulated loss and the theorem\'s rate, switched off outside the range, agree within {100 * abs(v[\'sim\'] / v[\'theory\'] - 1):.1f} percent."': "检验二：集中头寸。<bookmark mark='a'/>沿着同类路径的一个从六十到一百六十的区间，{100 * v['in_range']:.0f}%的时间在区间内。<bookmark mark='b'/>模拟的损失与定理在区间外关闭的速率相差不到{100 * abs(v['sim'] / v['theory'] - 1):.1f}%。",
    'f"Check the discrete data comparison. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> On ether\'s twenty twenty-three minute closes, the sum of step losses divided by changing starting pool values is {lv[\'lvr_pct\']:.2f} percent, versus {lv[\'rv8_pct\']:.2f} percent for squared log increments over eight. Monthly normalized loss sums range from {lo:.2f} to {hi:.2f} percent in this sample. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Exact discrete accounting needs positive prices and the stated rebalancing convention; interpreting squared log increments through the continuous rate uses a small-step approximation and continuous-price assumptions. Minute closes omit within-minute moves and can include market noise. Similar rounded totals do not independently validate those assumptions or establish an executable return."': "检查离散数据比较。<bookmark mark='a'/> 以太币2023年分钟收盘价中，单步损失除以变化的初始池价值再求和为 {lv['lvr_pct']:.2f}%，平方对数增量除以八为 {lv['rv8_pct']:.2f}%。月度归一化损失和从 {lo:.2f}% 到 {hi:.2f}%。<bookmark mark='b'/> 精确离散记账需要正价格及指定再平衡口径；用连续速率解释平方对数增量还需小步近似与连续价格假设。分钟收盘漏掉分钟内波动，并可能含市场噪声。相似四舍五入总量不独立验证假设，也不确立可执行收益。",
    "Now use a separate stationary reset model. <bookmark mark='a'/> Mispricing z is log external price over pool price. Between blocks, assume z has driftless Brownian increments of scale sigma. This is a log-price assumption, distinct from a martingale price level. <bookmark mark='b'/> For proportional input fee f, the exact symmetric log half-band is gamma equal to minus log one minus f. The small-fee approximation replaces gamma by f. <bookmark mark='c'/> Blocks arrive independently at Poisson rate lambda. <bookmark mark='d'/> A block outside the band resets z to the nearest edge. Inside, nothing resets it. Fixed blocks, log drift, jumps, discrete liquidity and transaction costs change this model.": "现在换一个平稳重置模型。<bookmark mark='a'/> 错价z为外部价格除以池价的对数。块间假设z具有尺度sigma的无漂移布朗增量；这是对数价格假设，不同于价格水平为鞅。<bookmark mark='b'/> 输入费率f给精确对称对数半带宽gamma等于负log一减f，小费用近似才用f代gamma。<bookmark mark='c'/> 区块以独立泊松率lambda到达。<bookmark mark='d'/> 若块到时在带外，z重置到最近边缘；带内不动。固定块、对数漂移、跳跃、离散流动性和成本都会改模型。",
    "The stationary law for the stated reset model. <bookmark mark='a'/> Inside the band, zero drift and symmetry reduce the stationary equation to a second derivative of zero, giving constant density c. <bookmark mark='b'/> Outside, Poisson resets remove density at rate lambda, giving exponential tails with rate a equal to square root of two lambda divided by sigma. Continuity and probability-flux balance connect the tails to the interior at both edges. <bookmark mark='c'/> Normalization gives c equal to one over twice gamma plus twice over a. <bookmark mark='d'/> Independent Poisson arrivals see stationary time averages, so the pre-block outside probability is one over one plus a gamma. This is exact for this stationary driftless-log reset model; substituting proportional fee f for gamma is an approximation.": "指定重置模型的平稳律。<bookmark mark='a'/> 带内零漂移与对称性使二阶导数为零，密度为常数c。<bookmark mark='b'/> 带外泊松重置以lambda速率移除密度，尾部指数衰减率a为根号二lambda除以sigma。密度连续与概率流平衡连接两侧边界。<bookmark mark='c'/> 归一化给c等于一除以二gamma加二除以a。<bookmark mark='d'/> 独立泊松到达看到平稳时间平均，因此到块前带外概率为一除以一加a gamma。精确性属于此平稳无对数漂移重置模型；用比例费率f代对数带宽gamma只是近似。",
    "Separate probability from profit. <bookmark mark='a'/> In the driftless-log Poisson reset model, trade probability is one over one plus eta, with eta equal to log half-band times square root of two lambda over sigma. Replacing the log half-band by proportional fee is a small-fee approximation. Relating arbitrage profit to a fee-free continuous LVR rate is a leading-order result under the paper's regularity and scaling. <bookmark mark='b'/> A fee changes the pool's trades and holdings, so it does not leave every finite-sample benchmark loss unchanged. In our outside-curve fee simulator, fee-inclusive rebalancing shortfall can be reconciled with arbitrage profit, while fee-free discrete LVR is a different comparison denominator. No general exact invariance follows.": "概率与利润分开。<bookmark mark='a'/> 无漂移对数泊松重置模型中，交易概率是一除以一加eta，eta为对数半带宽乘根号二lambda除以sigma。用比例费用代对数带宽是小费用近似。套利利润与无费连续损失速率的关系，是论文正则性及缩放下的主阶结果。<bookmark mark='b'/> 费用改变池交易与持仓，并不让每个有限样本基准损失不变。曲线外费用模拟里，含费再平衡缺口可与套利利润核对，无费离散损失却是另一个比较分母。不能推出一般精确不变性。",
    'f"Check the simulator\'s Poisson-clock comparisons with their assumptions visible. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The research histogram uses diffusion scale {t[\'sigma\']:.3f} per square root of one mean block unit. The plotted symmetric density assumes zero log drift, whereas the simulated exponential price has the negative half-variance log drift needed for a martingale level. Finite samples and window truncation also matter; close curves are an approximation check. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> At fee {100 * t[\'fee\']:.1f} percent, observed trade frequency is {t[\'p_trade\']:.3f}, versus {t[\'theory\']:.3f} using the proportional-fee approximation. The separate multi-fee experiment chooses eighty percent annual volatility and mean twelve-second blocks. Profit divided by fee-free discrete LVR is a different statistic from trade frequency."': "检查泊松时钟模拟，明确假设。<bookmark mark='a'/> 研究直方图扩散尺度为每平方根平均块单位 {t['sigma']:.3f}。对称密度假设零对数漂移，模拟指数价格却采用使价格水平为鞅的负半方差对数漂移。有限样本与窗口截断也重要，曲线接近只是近似检查。<bookmark mark='b'/> 费率 {100 * t['fee']:.1f}% 时，观测交易频率 {t['p_trade']:.3f}，比例费用近似给 {t['theory']:.3f}。另一个多费率实验指定年波动80%、平均12秒一块。利润除以无费离散损失，不同于交易频率统计量。",
    'f"Change the block clock. Ethereum has twelve-second slots after the Merge, but some slots are missed and actual execution includes more than a clock. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> In the chosen fixed-block simulation at three-tenths-percent fee, arbitrage profit divided by fee-free discrete LVR is {f3[\'arb_lvr\']:.3f}, versus {f3[\'theory\']:.3f} for the Poisson small-fee benchmark. Fixed times and exponential waiting times have different overshoot distributions, so agreement is not required. This descriptive comparison does not validate actual Ethereum execution or identify an exact universal ordering of all fee effects."': "改变区块时钟。合并后以太坊有12秒时隙，但会漏块，实际执行也不只是时钟。<bookmark mark='a'/> 指定固定块模拟中，0.3%费率的套利利润除以无费离散损失为 {f3['arb_lvr']:.3f}，泊松小费用基准为 {f3['theory']:.3f}。固定时刻与指数等待有不同越界分布，因此不要求一致。描述比较不验证真实以太坊执行，也不识别所有费用效应的普遍精确排序。",
    'f"Use ether\'s actual minute-close path as an external input to the unchanged fee simulator. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> At three-tenths-percent fee, simulated arbitrage profit divided by the fee-free discrete loss sum is {f3[\'arb_lvr\']:.2f}; relative to the displayed leading-order Brownian comparison it is about {ratio:.1f} times as large. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> That discrepancy is descriptive. Jumps, volatility clustering, log drift, sampling, finite fees and a changed pool state can all affect it. The close data do not isolate fat tails as the cause or prove that a Brownian theorem applies unchanged to this market. Fees are paid outside a fixed curve here and token fees are immediately valued in numeraire; native retained-fee compounding, gas and execution competition are omitted."': "将以太币实际分钟收盘路径输入费用模拟。<bookmark mark='a'/> 0.3%费率时，模拟套利利润除以无费离散损失和为 {f3['arb_lvr']:.2f}，约为所示主阶布朗比较的 {ratio:.1f} 倍。<bookmark mark='b'/> 差异只是描述。跳跃、波动聚集、对数漂移、采样、有限费用及池状态变化都可能影响结果。收盘数据不单独识别厚尾原因，也不证明布朗定理不变地适用。这里费用在固定曲线外，代币费用即时按计价币估值；原生费用复投、gas与执行竞争未建模。",
    "What the accounting suggests. <bookmark mark='a'/> Compare LP performance with both holding and a clearly defined self-financing rebalancing benchmark. Under a continuous fee-free model, the loss is a curvature-weighted quadratic-variation integral; real fee-inclusive trading needs its own ledger. <bookmark mark='b'/> Fee and auction design can change trading incentives, activity and allocation. Neither a static fee nor an auction is proved to recover a fixed universal amount by the examples here. <bookmark mark='c'/> A perpetual hedge adds funding, basis, collateral and execution costs. Fees minus idealized LVR is one component, rather than a complete net LP investment return.": "记账提示什么？<bookmark mark='a'/> 同时用持有及明确定义的自融资再平衡基准比较LP表现。连续无费模型中，损失为曲率加权二次变差积分；真实含费交易需要自己的账。<bookmark mark='b'/> 费用及拍卖可改变激励、活动与分配；例子不证明静态费或拍卖能普遍收回固定金额。<bookmark mark='c'/> 永续对冲加入资金费、基差、抵押品和执行成本。费用减理想LVR只是一个组成部分，不是完整净LP投资回报。",
    "Where this sits. <bookmark mark='a'/> Milionis, Moallemi, Roughgarden and Zhang defined LVR and proved the rate; Milionis, Moallemi and Roughgarden added fees and blocks. <bookmark mark='b'/> Agostino Capponi and Ruizhe Jia studied the fee's trade-off between providers and arbitrageurs, and Andreas Lehar and Christine Parlour who provides liquidity on Uniswap. <bookmark mark='c'/> And Angeris, Chitra and coauthors developed the convex geometry of these markets, their oracles and their routing.": "这项工作的位置。<bookmark mark='a'/>Milionis、Moallemi、Roughgarden和Zhang定义了LVR并证明了它的速率；Milionis、Moallemi和Roughgarden加入了手续费和区块。<bookmark mark='b'/>Agostino Capponi和Ruizhe Jia研究了手续费在提供者与套利者之间的权衡，Andreas Lehar和Christine Parlour研究了谁在Uniswap上提供流动性。<bookmark mark='c'/>Angeris、Chitra及合作者发展了这些市场的凸几何、它们的预言机和路由。",
    "Three research directions, framed by the cited literature rather than claimed absent from all later work. <bookmark mark='a'/> Extend fee-band comparisons to jumps, state-dependent volatility and execution costs; separate their effects empirically instead of attributing every residual to tails. <bookmark mark='b'/> Compare dynamic fees and auctions of arbitrage rights with strategic participants and measurable LP welfare. <bookmark mark='c'/> Study routing among many pools with different fees and ranges, including liquidity migration and competition. Existing papers address parts of these questions; the lecture's simplified simulator does not settle the general problems or establish the latest frontier.": "三个研究方向以所引文献为框架，不声称后续研究全未处理。<bookmark mark='a'/> 将费用带比较扩展到跳跃、状态波动和执行成本，经验上分离效果，而非把所有残差归因厚尾。<bookmark mark='b'/> 在策略参与者及可衡量LP福利下比较动态费与套利权拍卖。<bookmark mark='c'/> 研究不同费率、区间的多池路由、流动性迁移与竞争。已有论文处理部分问题，本讲简化模拟不解决一般问题，也不确立最新前沿。",
    "Pause and predict. A constant-product pool's volatility doubles, with the fee and the block rate unchanged. What happens to its loss-versus-rebalancing, and to the share of it arbitrageurs keep, if eta was one?": '暂停并预测。一个恒定乘积池的波动率翻倍，手续费和区块速率不变。如果原来eta等于一，它的相对再平衡损失会怎样？套利者拿走的份额又会怎样？',
    'Six definitions and measurements. Custodial venues and contracts on chain have different exposures. A fee-adjusted swap invariant differs from a reserve product that grows with retained fees. Holding and self-financing rebalancing answer different questions. The ether figures are changing-denominator normalized sums, compared with a small-step squared-log relation. Concentration scales local curvature, while realized fee income also depends on time in range and competition. The learned provider is a contextual-bandit experiment in an assumed world, without a claim of live investment performance.': '六项定义与衡量。托管场所与链上合约有不同暴露。考虑费用的交换不变量，不同于保留费用而增长的储备乘积。持有与自融资再平衡回答不同问题。以太币数字是分母变化的局部归一化和，与小步平方对数关系比较。集中放大局部曲率，实际费用还依赖区间内时间及竞争。学得提供者是指定世界的上下文赌博机实验，不声称实盘投资表现。',
    'Seven interpretation checks. A largest-feasible attack is not automatically profit-optimal. A simple funding annualization is not a strategy return on committed capital. Matched-unit carry still has basis, funding, collateral, venue and execution risks. The quarter-capital venue loss is a chosen zero-recovery stress. A USDC quote in tether is not a direct dollar redemption valuation. The stationary fee-band probability and the leading-order profit comparison have distinct assumptions. Finally, the proposed House rule organizes research and exposures; the lecture supplies no deployment or capital approval.': '七项解释检查。最大可行攻击不自动利润最优。简单资金费年化不是投入资本策略收益。匹配单位仍有基差、资金费、抵押品、场所和执行风险。四分之一资本损失是指定零回收压力。USDT计价的USDC不是直接美元赎回估值。平稳费用带概率与主阶利润比较假设不同。最后，拟议规则组织研究与暴露，本讲不提供部署或资本批准。',
    "Three connections. <bookmark mark='a'/> The familiar tools return in new mechanisms: a pool follows a swap rule, a perpetual has a funding clock and a reserve-backed token has issuer and redemption risks. <bookmark mark='b'/> Choose the benchmark for the question. Holding and self-financing rebalancing measure different gaps, and a real hedge adds costs. <bookmark mark='c'/> Market returns alone need not reveal custody, contracts, collateral transfers or redemption access. A research design needs those operational exposures alongside its price model, without assuming any one reported return series is complete.": "三个联系。<bookmark mark='a'/> 熟悉工具以新机制回来：池遵循交换规则，永续有资金费时钟，储备支持代币有发行人与赎回风险。<bookmark mark='b'/> 按问题选基准。持有和自融资再平衡衡量不同缺口，真实对冲会加成本。<bookmark mark='c'/> 市场收益未必揭示托管、合约、抵押品转移或赎回通道。研究设计要把操作暴露与价格模型并列，不假定任何收益序列完整。",
    "The part on one card. Impermanent loss. The LVR rate and its constant-product form. The exact one-step loss. The capital efficiency of a range. The trade probability with fees and blocks, and arbitrage profit. And the perpetual's no-arbitrage price.": '一张卡片上的这一部分。无常损失。LVR速率及其恒定乘积形式。精确的单步损失。区间的资本效率。带手续费和区块的交易概率，以及套利利润。还有永续合约的无套利价格。',
    "How this part connects. <bookmark mark='a'/> Backwards: Part thirty-eight's stale quote is a pool's stale price, Part eleven's short gamma is a provider's, Part twenty-two's carry is funding, and Part two's margin account is the perpetual's. <bookmark mark='b'/> Sideways: Part twenty-one's counterparty risk is venue risk, and Part nine's futures are the perpetual's dated cousins. <bookmark mark='c'/> Forwards: Part forty measures risk in a market with fat tails and no close, Part forty-one's spirals ran through crypto in twenty twenty-two, and Part forty-two's machines include its bots.": "这一部分如何与其他部分相连。<bookmark mark='a'/>往回看：第38部分的过时报价就是池子的过时价格，第11部分的负伽马就是提供者的负伽马，第22部分的套息就是资金费率，第2部分的保证金账户就是永续合约的保证金账户。<bookmark mark='b'/>横向看：第21部分的交易对手风险就是交易场所风险，第9部分的期货是永续合约有到期日的亲戚。<bookmark mark='c'/>往前看：第40部分在一个有肥尾、不收盘的市场里测量风险，第41部分的螺旋在2022年贯穿了加密市场，第42部分的机器包括它的机器人。",
    "Three pool questions. Price doubles in a fee-free constant-product pool: relative to terminal holding value the gap is minus five point seven two percent. <bookmark mark='a'/> The continuous rebalancing gap is a curvature-weighted quadratic-variation integral with common initial wealth and regularity assumptions. <bookmark mark='b'/> Narrowing a range scales local curvature, but cannot guarantee better net performance when volume, competition, exits and costs also change.": "三个池问题。无费常数乘积池价格翻倍，相对期末持有价值差为负5.72%。<bookmark mark='a'/> 连续再平衡缺口为共同初值和正则性下的曲率加权二次变差积分。<bookmark mark='b'/> 缩窄区间放大局部曲率，但成交量、竞争、出界和成本也变，不能保证净表现提高。",
    "Three institutional questions. Funding incentives help link a perpetual to spot, subject to constraints and the contract's rules. <bookmark mark='a'/> Matched-unit carry retains basis, funding, margin, custody and venue risks. <bookmark mark='b'/> A stablecoin quote below a reserve stress does not identify its cause. Reserve valuation, other claims, redemption rights, timing and quote currency all matter. The notes give the assumptions behind each answer.": "三个制度问题。资金费激励帮助联系永续与现货，受约束与合约规则限制。<bookmark mark='a'/> 匹配单位保留基差、资金费、保证金、托管及场所风险。<bookmark mark='b'/> 稳定币报价低于储备压力不识别原因。储备估值、其他请求权、赎回权、时序与计价币都重要。讲义给出每题假设。",
    "The research pause is conditional on the model. <bookmark mark='a'/> At the same price and pool state, doubling instantaneous sigma quadruples the fee-free local LVR rate. A realized whole-path loss need not be exactly four times. <bookmark mark='b'/> In the stationary driftless-log Poisson model, eta halves from one to one half, so trade probability rises from one half to two thirds. The leading-order profit comparison would scale by sixteen thirds relative to the original arbitrage profit, if its additional regularity and asymptotic approximation apply. It is not an exact finite-fee statement about all LP losses or fees.": "研究暂停题的答案以模型为条件。<bookmark mark='a'/> 同价同池状态下，即时sigma翻倍，无费局部LVR速率翻四倍；整条实现路径损失不必恰为四倍。<bookmark mark='b'/> 平稳无对数漂移泊松模型中，eta从一减半到二分之一，交易概率由二分之一升至三分之二。若额外正则性和渐近近似成立，主阶利润比较给相对原套利利润十六除以三倍。这不是任意LP损失和费用的精确有限费用结论。",
    "Twelve problems with complete bilingual solutions. Six basic problems cover relative impermanent loss, an exact curve trade, local dollar loss rates, a discrete doubling, multiplicative range efficiency and the exact log fee band. <bookmark mark='a'/> Four advanced problems distinguish simple funding return on committed capital, the continuous perpetual model, a fully specified failure-payoff calculation and sequential liquidation accounting. <bookmark mark='b'/> Two qualifying problems prove the continuous and discrete LVR identities with regularity and a jump extension, then derive the stationary reset density with flux balance, its probability limits and the conditions needed for profit comparisons. Each answer states its units and assumptions.": "十二道题有完整双语解答。六道基础题包括相对无常损失、精确曲线交易、局部美元损失速率、离散翻倍、乘法区间效率及精确对数费用带。<bookmark mark='a'/> 四道进阶题区分投入资本简单资金费收益、连续永续模型、明确失败支付的期望及顺序清算记账。<bookmark mark='b'/> 两道资格题在正则性下证明连续与离散LVR并扩展跳跃，再通过概率流平衡推导平稳重置密度、概率极限和利润比较所需条件。每个答案说明单位与假设。",
    "Where this comes back. Part forty measures risk in markets with fat tails and no close. Part forty-one follows leverage and liquidity spirals, of which crypto's twenty twenty-two was a chain. Part forty-two builds the machines that trade, quote and order blocks. And Part forty-three asks whether anyone can beat the market.": '这些内容会在哪里再出现。第40部分在有肥尾、不收盘的市场里测量风险。第41部分追踪杠杆和流动性螺旋，加密市场的2022年就是一条连锁反应。第42部分构建交易、报价和安排区块的机器。第43部分追问是否有人能战胜市场。',
    'The notes connect the textbook chapters with primary papers and their assumptions, including the loss-versus-rebalancing identity and fee-band model. Computed ordinary outputs, chosen accounting examples and cited historical facts have distinct labels. The market samples do not turn the idealized simulator into a verified executable strategy, and historical legal milestones do not certify current product terms.': '讲义把教材章节与原始论文及假设相连，包括再平衡损失恒等式和费用带模型。常规计算输出、指定算术例子及有出处的历史事实分别标注。市场样本不让理想模拟成为已验证可执行策略，历史法律节点也不认证当前产品条款。',
    "Act six has built the tools to study dealers, books, execution, market making and on-chain mechanisms. The digital-assets desk remains a proposed research design with unresolved operational and investment validation. <bookmark mark='a'/> Next, Act seven studies the system. Part forty measures risk with value at risk and expected shortfall, and asks how to tell whether a risk model works.": "第六幕建立了研究交易商、订单簿、执行、做市与链上机制的工具。数字资产交易台仍是研究提案，操作和投资验证尚未解决。<bookmark mark='a'/> 接下来第七幕研究系统。第四十部分用风险价值和预期损失衡量风险，并问如何判断风险模型是否有效。",
}
